Adarsh, how do you evaluate a software engineer’s technical skills during the initial screening stage? What questions or methods do you typically use?', '2026-05-01 22:14:24.167', 59, null), ('cmovxdmek007tn20kudcfolh2', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello, can you hear me?', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 0, null), ('cmovxdmek007un20kl2zcxop1', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Mangesh, yes, I can hear you clearly. Let’s begin. My name is the interviewer for today’s session. Let’s start with a quick introduction. Can you give me a brief snapshot of your professional background, the technologies you’ve worked with, and your domain experience?', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 1, null), ('cmovxdmek007vn20klwpm639w', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, sure, I have 18 years of experience and out of those 18 years, I have worked on Java for 14 years. I have worked on Spring, Spring Boot, Spring Security, Spring JDBC, Spring MVC, Spring Data, and I have also worked on the creation of microservices, API. I migrated monolithic application to the microservices application. I have architecture experience and I have team lead experience and technical. I have also worked on the, worked as a technical SME. I worked in the front-end using React.js, AngularJS, and TypeScript, JavaScript, CSS, HTML. I used them in the front-end. I have used Oracle, SQL Server, MySQL, MongoDB in the back-end, in the database side.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 2, null), ('cmovxdmek007wn20kxe68o8zy', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'And I have also worked on various repositories like GitHub repository, GitHub repository, GitHub repository, then I have worked on creation of pipelines like the Jenkins, then Azure pipelines, AWS core pipelines. I have worked on the cloud. I got exposure on GCP, Azure, and AWS.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 3, null), ('cmovxdmek007xn20kxb9769wd', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'From the AWS side, I have worked on CodeCommit, CodeBuild, CodePipeline, and EC2, serverless deployment, Lambda, then SNS, S3 bucket.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 4, null), ('cmovxdmek007yn20ki9u3ockj', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'And in the EKS as well as ECS, so I have worked on the Docker or containerization of images. I have worked on the Kubernetes for orchestration of the images.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 5, null), ('cmovxdmek007zn20kw55yltes', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'And yeah, I also work on the project management tools like Jira, Ali, Azure Boards, and Confluence, SharePoint also, and I use a bit of copilot for code optimization, removing the code, boilerplate code to enhance the code, that is about my production.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 6, null), ('cmovxdmek0080n20krabl2f25', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that comprehensive overview. Now, let’s dive a bit deeper into the role. Can you tell me about your experience specifically with Angular—what versions have you used, and what kind of work have you done on the frontend with it?', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 7, null), ('cmovxdmek0081n20ksje4dudz', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'I have worked on Angular 15 and Angular 16. I created a usable components like profile components, many components. And then I have also worked on other components which are responsive. So we have used material UI also to get the responsive UI on different browsers and different devices. Then I have worked on the address signal so that only specific DOM binding is updated.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 8, null), ('cmovxdmek0082n20kccc3rrqa', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'Then I have worked on the Irix.js along with the Angular to consume the APIs and and display the data to the browser.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 9, null), ('cmovxdmek0083n20k87cy0nd0', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, that gives me a solid picture of your Angular experience. Now, can you walk me through an example where you integrated an Angular frontend with a Spring Boot backend, including how you handled security and state management?', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 10, null), ('cmovxdmek0084n20kmhsuoq9h', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'So Spring Boot is used to create the microservices and if we talk about the security, we can use JWT or OAuth to secure the APIs. So we can use JWT alone. We can customize the JWT or we can use OAuth and generate the token using OAuth. So there are different OAuth providers like Azure, Azure is there, Microsoft Azure, then Google is there, Facebook is there, GitHub is there. So these are a few providers you can make use to authenticate, authorize the user. And we can also use the JWT and OAuth combination. And to secure the APIs, we can pass these tokens. We can pass this token to Azure gateway or AWS gateway, which authenticate the URL and they fetch the token from the header part of the URL and authenticate the request.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 11, null), ('cmovxdmek0085n20k1azpangz', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'So this way you can authenticate the APIs and we can integrate the Spring Boot APIs. First we can create the Spring Boot APIs and to create the Spring Boot APIs, we need to create the schema first. Then when we get our schema Smale ready, we can go to Spring initializer and create a project there, download the dependencies or add the dependencies into the form.xml and download the project as a zip file and extract the zip file and import the project into the Eclipse or any other integrated tool or any other tool. And from then we can start the coding development. So we can create, we can start creating the entity classes like we can start creating the', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 12, null), ('cmovxdmek0086n20kzdoic78x', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'Repository class is a service class is a risk controller, and we can', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 13, null), ('cmovxdmek0087n20kde220xom', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'How to wire up the repository into service and the repository into the rest controller and in the rest controller you can add the CRUD level operations like get is there, put is there, post is there, patch is there, delete is there. You can have all those methods implemented.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 14, null), ('cmovxdmek0088n20k99nywg20', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'And we can build up the single application and test the APIs. Let''s say if we have a product schema already and we have scheduled operation for the product, we can test the product either from Swagger or Postman. And then once they are tested, we can continue with the application enhancement.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 15, null), ('cmovxdmek0089n20kfdexd95m', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now, how did you manage state on the Angular side for these secured APIs—did you use something like NgRx or another approach?', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 16, null), ('cmovxdmek008an20k172a61gg', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, NGRX can be used for the state management. We can manage the state of the component in Angular as well as in React also we can manage the state.', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 17, null), ('cmovxdmek008bn20kcdsu5dvj', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for clarifying. Now, can you share an example of a challenging issue you faced in integrating an Angular frontend with a Spring Boot backend, and how you resolved it?', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 18, null), ('cmovxdmek008cn20k0rlefoqn', 'cmovwyez2007rn20kdpop2qmw', 'CANDIDATE', 'Um...', '2026-05-07 20:15:00.524', 19, null), ('cmowai9my008kn20kcscephgi', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'CANDIDATE', 'I don''t do hear anything.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 0, null), ('cmowai9my008ln20k7qbbmfdx', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Nikhil, let me introduce myself. I’m here to conduct your technical interview for the Java Developer role. Let’s get started by having you give me a quick overview of your professional background—technologies you’ve worked with and your domain experience. Then we’ll go deeper from there.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 1, null), ('cmowai9my008mn20kc4ybf57u', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure. Coming to me, I''m Nikhil Rao. I have overall 12 plus years of experience into IT, which includes both front-end and back-end. And I''m currently working with Freddie Mac. On the back-end, I''m working with Java Springboard and microservices with REST and SOAP APIs. And on the front-end, I do have experience with the CSS, JavaScript, React, Angular. So in the Freddie Mac, I worked on a mortgage and loan processing platform. So the business goal of the system was to help internal users to process the mortgage loan applications and validate the borrower information and integrate with third-party financial systems and perform eligibility checks and track loan status through different workflow strategies. And currently, I''m working in agile methodology. So we have a two-week sprint, and based on capacity planning, the number of story points, the stories will be assigned to me and I will work on them and I will make sure they are 100% done, like writing the unit test cases, integration test cases, end-to-end test cases, business functionality. Everything should be available to go for the production. So once the development is completed within two weeks, I will push that into the production. Based on split flags, whether that feature needs to be enabled or disabled will be decided. This is what currently whatever I am doing.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 2, null), ('cmowai9my008nn20k5t06k988', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that overview. Now, let’s dig a bit deeper. Can you tell me about your experience with Angular specifically—what versions have you worked on and what kinds of Angular projects', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 3, null), ('cmowai9my008on20k8ewx2fu8', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'CANDIDATE', 'Great.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 4, null), ('cmowai9my008pn20kjjnv5sdn', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Could you share a bit more detail about the Angular versions you''ve used and the specific features or modules you''ve implemented?', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 5, null), ('cmowai9my008qn20kfi0inyjm', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, so coming to the Angular versions, I do have experience with the Angular 17 right now, and before that, I worked with Angular 9 and Angular Plain.js also. And coming to the modules and components, I developed the dashboard and different components like table and selects and like different components from the Angular I did use. And those are used on the UI by fetching the data from the backend and displaying it on the UI. And I mostly followed the model-based plus component-driven architecture. And so I have models like different models, customer model, dashboard and admin transactions, and shared components in that components, services, interceptors, guards, guards for routing, and core models. I do have like authorization config and models. So this is the structure I did used, and each one has its, what you can say, HTML component and a TypeScript component, and accordingly, I did develop the components in the Angular.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 6, null), ('cmowai9my008rn20kmvei1n32', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Thanks for that. Now, how do you typically manage state in your Angular applications—do you use NgRx, Signals, or any other state management approach?', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 7, null), ('cmowai9my008sn20kjgkcsfx9', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood, that’s a solid approach. Now, can you tell me how you''ve handled complex asynchronous data flows in your Angular applications, especially with NgRx?', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 8, null), ('cmowai9my008tn20kt4midvlf', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, so to manage state in Angular application, currently I''m using what you can say ngrx and so with the help of the ngrx, what you can say the components store we are using. And so inside the store, what you can say this state we are maintaining in the Angular application, like whenever the user logged in or transactions are performing or there are different, different operations. Based on different, different operations, I''m storing the data. So coming to ngrx, it gives me centralized state management and predictable data flow and no one can modify the state without proper flow triggering. Yeah, so that''s the reason I''m using this. And here I have a component architecture like component and dispatching the action and reducers to generate the new state and then store updated from there and then selector will supply the whatever the new state is there to the component, which basically re-render and visible to the user. The store is which is centralized application state and actions which describe actually what happened or what action did by the user. And those are immutable events and reducers are pure functions which updates the states and effects. We can have the side effects like handling asynchronous operations like REST API calls or Kafka WebSocket updates. And then we have selectors which are used to read optimized slices of the state. These are the components I did used from the ngrx for the Angular state operations.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 9, null), ('cmowai9my008un20ky6nmaqg0', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'CANDIDATE', 'Complex asynchronous data operations in using NgRx means in the current application, we are doing the API calls and we are getting the data. And for that, we are using the observables where we are subscribing and getting the data. So these tasks, or I can say to handle asynchronously, we are doing multiple parallel API calls to reduce the, what you can say, time we actually doing to render the data and catching the data and retry mechanism. So where if we see the dashboard, so on the dashboard, we have number of API calls to load the profile, transactions, and API call permissions, and all these things, we have number of calls on the dashboard. So definitely we need parallel API calls. For that, I am using the fork join from the NgRx. So with the help of the fork join, I''m doing the multiple calls and then whenever I am getting the response from everything, I am joining with the pipe and then I am mapping the response accordingly, whatever the response I am getting. And as all APIs are independent, there is no function calls to one to another. So I can call them parallely with this fork join. And apart from that, like switch map also I''m using whenever it basically considers only new requests, the switch map. So that''s the reason I''m going with this switch map when I need a transactions using the customer ID and which cancels the previous API request. Apart from that, we do have exhaust map and queue requests. These are some of the ways I can handle asynchronous data operations using the NgRx in my Angular.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 10, null), ('cmowai9my008vn20kvvbu8ec9', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks, Nikhil, that’s clear. One final question: how do you ensure application security in your full stack development?', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 11, null), ('cmowai9my008wn20kiefwvkom', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, so to ensure the application security, I''m using what you can say, authorization token mechanism. There we are using the bearer token. So with the help of the bearer token, whenever the application user tried or logged into the application, then there is an API called for the authentication and authorization. And with the credentials, whatever the user given, that will be carried to authorization server. And for that server, it will validate that user credentials. If the credentials are valid, then the JWT token generated and supplied to the UI. And every time whenever next time UI is trying to do an API call to the backend, that token will be supplied in the authorization header and that will be validated with the authorization server. And if the token is valid, then the request is allowed into the application and what we can say the request is serviced. And that''s how currently we are doing and that token is valid for 15 minutes. Once the token is expired, then server returns the 401 and then UI will call what I can say regenerate or refresh endpoint. And that refresh endpoint, what it will do is it will generate the new token and it will get that new token. And then for every other new request, that refresh token will be sent in the authorization header. That''s how currently we are handling security in my application.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 12, null), ('cmowai9my008xn20krqlik98b', 'cmowa44xw008in20k88abcm5n', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Good. Thanks for that explanation, Nikhil. That covers everything I needed. We’ll be in touch soon. Take care.', '2026-05-08 02:22:32.266', 13, null), ('cmowvnecn0095n20k7zahsm6c', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 0, null), ('cmowvnecn0096n20kvxhslndb', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Dhrupal. This is a professional interview for the Full Stack Java Developer role. Let''s dive in. Could you start by giving me a quick overview of your professional background, the technologies you''ve worked with, and your domain experience?', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 1, null), ('cmowvnecn0097n20kzgqdwx6p', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, I have over 12 years plus experience in software development, mainly in the JavaScript development. My core expertise is in Java, J2EE, Spring, and front-end frameworks like Angular, React, and AngularJS. I have worked with a database such as Oracle, MySQL, and I have experience with both SQL and NoSQL databases like MongoDB and the NoSQL database. On the front-end side, I have used HTML, CSS, JavaScript, jQuery, Angular, and I have experience with cloud platforms like AWS and Azure, including using the services like Lambda, DynamoDB, and CloudFront.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 2, null), ('cmowvnecn0098n20kabs38v47', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that overview. Now, can you tell me about your most recent project where you worked with Java and Angular together?', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 3, null), ('cmowvnecn0099n20kmgv7p599', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, so in my current project, I''m working with a developer. I''m working with a senior Java full-stack developer, where I manage and develop a solution for the complex home mortgage loan liquidation, ensuring the compliance with the bank''s servicing guidelines and federal regulation. So in this project, I''m working with Java with Angular, and on the backend, I use Java and Spring Boot to build and upgrade internal and external applications for the mortgage origination process. For the front-end, I develop user interface using Angular, focusing on creating efficient and component-based screens for both internal teams, as well as end users.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 4, null), ('cmowvnecn009an20kw7f32gfb', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How did you handle state management in that Angular application?', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 5, null), ('cmowvnecn009bn20k8oeqbbpt', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, for state management in the Angular application, I use the Angular service to share data and manage the state across the different components. In more complex scenarios, I implemented the state management libraries like NgRX to handle the global state, especially for larger applications with multiple modules. And also, I use the local storage and session storage for persisting user data and temporary information across the sub of the pages or the routes.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 6, null), ('cmowvnecn009cn20k6mo8om5v', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How do you typically ensure security in your Spring Boot backends, especially around authentication and authorization?', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 7, null), ('cmowvnecn009dn20kl6s4shla', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I use Spring Security as the main framework to handle authentication and authorization in Spring Boot application. For authentication, I often implement the JWT token or OAuth2 depending on the project requirement to securely verify user identity. And I configure role-based access control using an annotation like @PreAuthorize and @Secured to restrict access to specific endpoints based on the user roles. Sensitive endpoints are protected by required authentication, and I use HTTPS to encrypt data in transit. And passwords are always stored securely using a strong hashing algorithm like a bcrypt.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 8, null), ('cmowvnecn009en20kvobuj6xb', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for clarifying. Now, how do you approach optimizing performance in a high-traffic Angular application?', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 9, null), ('cmowvnecn009fn20k51ykmu1j', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, I use Angular''s Ahead-of-Time compilation to reduce the bundle size and improve the load time. I implement a lazy loading for modules so that only necessary code is loaded when needed. This speed up initial load, and I use Angular''s change detection strategy on push to minimize unnecessary component re-renders.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 10, null), ('cmowvnecn009gn20k44cehv04', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. One last question: how do you typically integrate a CI/CD pipeline for your Java and Angular projects?', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 11, null), ('cmowvnecn009hn20k0rm3cylm', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'So typically, I set up a CI/CD pipeline using tools like Jenkins and CircleCI or in the AWS CodePipeline depending on the project and cloud environment. For version control, I use a Git repository such as a Bitbucket or GitHub or GitHub to manage the source code for both the Java and Angular projects. The pipeline is triggered automatically on code commits, on pull requests for the backend. I use a Maven or Gradle to build the project, run unit and integration tests, and generate artifacts like a JAR or WAR file. For the front-end Angular, I use an Angular CLI to build and run the test and produce the optimized static files. And the pipeline includes steps for static code analysis and quality checks using the tools like SonarQube.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 12, null), ('cmowvnecn009in20knvzi90ag', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you, Dhrupal. That covers what we needed. We''ll be in touch. Take care.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 13, null), ('cmowvnecn009jn20keoyu6404', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', '这个谢谢。', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 14, null), ('cmowvnecn009kn20k24y7s6od', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'You''re welcome. Have a great day ahead. Goodbye.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 15, null), ('cmowvnecn009ln20kedn6fm4i', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'You do. Thank you.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 16, null), ('cmowvnecn009mn20k64ixmrfm', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. Take care.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 17, null), ('cmowvnecn009nn20kwmbony4a', 'cmowvev7g0093n20khwca0asq', 'CANDIDATE', 'Goodbye.', '2026-05-08 12:14:23.592', 18, null), ('cmox08dlz009vn20k5uv7nm2k', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'I can''t hear anything.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 0, null), ('cmox08dlz009wn20kkibf0lhe', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for letting me know. I’ll adjust my volume and speak clearly. Let’s begin. Hi Sairam, I’m glad to meet you. We’re going to have a conversation about your experience as a Java Developer. Let’s start with a quick overview.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 1, null), ('cmox08dlz009xn20kg7u47fqb', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'OK.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 2, null), ('cmox08dlz009yn20k66ie5qjs', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right, let’s dive in. Can you give me a quick overview of your professional background, the key technologies you’ve worked with, and your domain experience?', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 3, null), ('cmox08dlz009zn20kb438tf1r', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'No.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 4, null), ('cmox08dlz00a0n20ki9lf208t', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right, let’s take it step by step. Can you give me a quick summary of your professional background, the key technologies you’ve worked with, and your domain experience?', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 5, null), ('cmox08dlz00a1n20kqlkasikf', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'I am a full-stack Java developer with six years of experience, mainly working in enterprise application development with a stronger focus on backend engineering. Most of my experience is with Java, Spring Boot microservices, and REST APIs, and database design, also coming to performance optimization and securing application development, along with frontend work using Angular and React when required. From a technology perspective, my core backend stack is Java. I have worked from versions 8 to the latest version 17 and 21, and Spring Boot and Spring MVC also I have used, and Spring Security, Spring Data JPA, Hibernate, REST APIs, and microservices. Most of my work was revolving around this. And on frontend, we used CSS for building reusable UI components and integrating with backend services. And for databases, I have worked with SQL Server and PostgreSQL, MySQL, and Oracle mostly. And also, I have a huge experience in using AWS services. And on cloud and DevOps, I have worked mostly with AWS and also have experience in Azure. And most of the services are like EKS, SQS, Lambda, CodePipeline, CloudWatch. I have used these. And I have also used Kubernetes and Jenkins, and also recently GitHub Actions and Terraform. And domain-wise, most of my experience is in financial services and banking, working with organizations like Barclays, Morgan Stanley, and recently TD Securities. I have worked on applications related to compliance workflows, internal banking platforms and reporting systems, and transaction processing, and enterprise workflow automation like this.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 6, null), ('cmox08dlz00a2n20k61oo6cli', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that detailed summary. Now, can you walk me through a specific project where you worked extensively with Angular on the front end?', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 7, null), ('cmox08dlz00a3n20kwmdw6csi', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay, sure. When I was working in Barclays, we were using an Angular project I worked on, like where the front end was used by internal users to view customer account details, search records, and update workflow status, and submit review actions. Mainly, I worked mainly on Angular components, TypeScript services, and API integration from handling validations and UI bug fixes. We had reusable components for tables, filters, dropdowns, and models. And also, we have used action buttons. So instead of writing up duplicate UI logic, we tried to keep the code modular. For API communication, we used Angular services like with the HTTP client and the service layer that calls Spring Boot REST APIs, and the components would subscribe to the response and bind the data to the UI. Like, for example, when a user searched an account, Angular would call the backend API with filter parameters and get the response and display it in a grid. And also, I have worked on reactive forms for validation-heavy screens. We used validators for required fields and date checks, dropdown selections, and comments also before, like, submitting any workflow action. Yeah.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 8, null), ('cmox08dlz00a4n20k2q2vsqgj', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, that’s helpful. How did you handle state management in that Angular project, especially for complex data flows?', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 9, null), ('cmox08dlz00a5n20khercgqh1', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, sure. When coming to state management, in that project, what we did is, like, we usually don''t keep everything inside components, like, I separate state into service level state, uh, share the observables and component level state depending on the scope. And also for simple screens, we used service-based state management with RxJS, mainly like a behavior subject or a replay subject, like that. Like, let''s take an example, like if multiple components need the selected account, like filters or user workflow status, I keep that in shared service. Components subscribe to it and whenever the value changes, the UI updates automatically. And for more complex flows, like search results and selected row or approval status and dependent drop-downs, we kept the API calls inside services and exposed observables streams to components. Like, that way, the component is not overloaded with the business logic. And also in some cases, if the application is huge and many modules share the same state, we preferred NgRx or a state-based approach. There we maintain actions, reducers, and effects. Also actions represented what happened, effects handle API calls and reducers update the state, and also we used selectors which give clean data back to the UI.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 10, null), ('cmox08dlz00a6n20kysmdcp1x', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for clarifying. Now, how did you handle error handling and debugging in those Angular services and components?', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 11, null), ('cmox08dlz00a7n20kjwytsimw', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood,', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 12, null), ('cmox08dlz00a8n20ko6s1q96k', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay, coming to the error handling and debugging, right, you have asked, okay, like what we used in that components is, like mainly, we used multiple levels instead of putting everything in the component. When it''s a component heavy, like at the service layer, we used handle API, like API related errors using RxJS, sorry, like with catch error, and that kept the HTTP error handling centralized and avoided the repeated same logic in every component. And for example, like if the backend returns 400 or 401 or 403 or internal errors like 500, I map those into meaningful messages or fallback handling. Something like this in practice, what we did, like mainly what we did is the service makes the API call, uses catch error, and logs the error if needed, and either throws a user-friendly error or returns a safe fallback response depending on the use case. And at the component level, we handled it like UI behavior, for example, like showing error messages, stopping loaders, disabling submit buttons, or allowing retry, these things we did. The component should care about user experience, not, I say, not low-level HTTP parsing. And for global handling, if the application has repeated authentication session issues, we used an HTTP interceptor, and that''s useful for handling token expiry and unauthorized access and adding the author headers or generic error logging. If a 401 comes back, then interceptor can redirect to login or trigger token refresh logic.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 13, null), ('cmox08dlz00a9n20kbtcudcru', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'CANDIDATE', 'That''s what I would say.', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 14, null), ('cmox08dlz00aan20kfiw8mp9d', 'cmowy0o8g009tn20kyp1yqroq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that. Now, can you describe a challenging performance issue you faced in a Spring Boot microservice and how you resolved it?', '2026-05-08 14:22:40.871', 15, null), ('cmox1yxv400ain20ktowu1mhx', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Marru, welcome. Let’s dive right in. Can you start by giving me a snapshot of your professional background, the technologies you''ve worked with, and your domain experience?', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 0, null), ('cmox1yxv400ajn20k05kspf12', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that overview. Let’s dig a little deeper into your current role. Can you tell me more about how you''re applying Angular in your projects right now?', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 1, null), ('cmox1yxv400akn20k80ne0qf2', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, sure. Let me quickly overview about me. I am Chindu Maru. I''ve been doing like a job with tech development for about like eight years now across like few different industries which have been cool, honestly. So right now I''m working at Comcast in Philly as a senior Java developer. I''ve been there like since October 2025, and you know, we are building like cloud native applications using Java 11, Python Spring Boot, and all running like on AWS. Like there is a pretty intense because so we are dealing with super high volume traffic, so event-driven architecture is kind of necessary. And we use Kafka heavily for processing between services. I''ve been working a lot of AWS Lambdas and also with DynamoDB and also step functions and also basically serverless and distributed system stuff. And also working with ELK stands for like a centralized logging, which has been like a lifesaver for instance. Before Comcast, I was like at the TD Bank in Mount Laurel for like about a year, like from September 2024 to September 2025. And then like I have been interested being dealing with the actual backlag transactions and also building spring boot microservices for like financial workflows and security as old spring security that also, we also use like AWS cases for like real-time event streaming and also built like some graphQL to reduce overfetching compared to REST. And which has been before that, I have been before that I have been like worked with wind supply in Dayton, Ohio, and also that has also has been retail supply chain and ASG that was my with season in Connecticut. That''s been like helped me like really about like new domains. Tech stack wise, my core tech stack is like Java, spring boot, and Hibernate and Spring Boot frameworks, and also JPA and also have a good with Angular and React frameworks and also with GraphQL and REST APIs. This is like an high level overview about me and I also did my master''s in computer science in New York in finished in like May 2023 and then later joined with supply.', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 2, null), ('cmox1yxv400aln20k8zmqvjf0', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, sure. Coming to uh let me clarify like uh we are like not heavily using Angular, but in my current project, like uh we are more into React.js, Python on the front-end side. Where do we like a UI work and honestly a lot of like I''m doing backend focus, Java, Spring Boot, AWS services, Kafka, that are a thing. And I also have like solid Angular experience from my previous roles, especially like Edwin supply. So Edwin Supply, I was building full Angular applications using TypeScript and material UI. Like we had like some of the internal dashboards for like supply chain management and inventory tracking and Angular component-based architecture was really nice for that because you could like uh build reusable UI components and two-way data binding and like forms really clean to work with. And honestly, I''ve been like more like a uh Angular person these days and React also. I''ve been more recently at TD Bank and built React.js UIs and Redux for state management and React Router for navigations. And Angular is catered like the concepts translate pretty well between two frameworks, you know, component lifecycle, state management, routing, different syntactics and patterns. So yeah. So definitely I have a good understanding and experience working with Angular. Yeah.', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 3, null), ('cmox1yxv400amn20kyfmcii5z', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood, sounds like you''ve got a strong Angular foundation from past projects. Now, how comfortable are you working with RxJS and state management libraries', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 4, null), ('cmox1yxv400ann20k9lvioc05', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Okay, let''s explore that a bit. Can you describe your experience using RxJS or similar reactive programming patterns?', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 5, null), ('cmox1yxv400aon20kd6svros2', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, so, yeah, coming to RxJS, like especially uh super heavy in like production, so you know, like concept of reactive programming and observabilities, but uh done with RxJS like in Angular projects, anything like that. So I have worked with reactive patterns and different concepts like, you know, like at Comcast and TD Bank. I''ve been driving like a event-driven architecture with Kafka and AWS services, which has been like a conceptually similar. And you are dealing with like streams of data and you know, like a synchronous processing and handling back pressure and so that mindset of reactive programming. Um And also using to rather than imperative control flow, that is definitely comfortable with. Uh So I am very familiar with like reactive and event-driven patterns on the back end with Kafka and Kinesis, and I also built a streaming UIs. If RxJS is something you guys have lead, you have been conforming like a I can pick and stream like a big part of the front end full stack.', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 6, null), ('cmox1yxv400apn20kcosxd03g', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, that sounds solid. Now, how have you approached implementing state management in your previous Angular projects?', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 7, null), ('cmox1yxv400aqn20kcmgzwlvd', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, if you would like coming to like Angular projects, especially when we are coming to wind supply was Angular the most. Actually, I kept like state management pretty straightforward, like for the applications I was building. So we don''t have like super complex global state management requirements. So I mostly rely on like Angular built-in services and component state rather than pulling in something like a NGRX, which is kind of Redux equivalent for Angular. So basically, I worked with created like singleton services using Angular, dependency injection, you know, that injectable decorator and provided in root and those services would like hold like shared state and business logic and components would inject like those services and subscribe to observables or just call methods. And it worked well for like uh what we need, like things like user session data, filter status for dashboards, and kind of thing. And that said, like I have been much deeper state management experience. This is like a full like a Angular experience, like I''m comfortable with. Yeah.', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 8, null), ('cmox1yxv400arn20kxr3wl58o', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks, that’s helpful. Let me ask one final question: how do you ensure the security of your Angular applications?', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 9, null), ('cmox1yxv400asn20ksd9ae6f1', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'CANDIDATE', '네?', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 10, null), ('cmox1yxv400atn20kirwg8pdz', 'cmox1irdc00agn20kvi6wmgjh', 'INTERVIEWER', 'How do you ensure application security when building both the frontend and the backend?', '2026-05-08 15:11:19.792', 11, null), ('cmox5g1bj00ban20kg31adp1x', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 0, null), ('cmox5g1bj00bbn20kkbgxfeww', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Sandhya, this is our interview for the Senior .NET Developer role. Let’s get started. Could you tell me a bit about your background and how it aligns with this role?', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 1, null), ('cmox5g1bj00bcn20kp6zjsb31', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, sure. So this is Sandhya. I''m a .NET developer, Senior .NET Full Stack Developer with 10 years of experience. Mostly I work with the, you know, the scalable applications like applications using Microsoft stack, primarily with the C Sharp, ASP.NET Core, .NET 6.7 blanks, Web APIs, and SQL Server. So over the years, I have worked across the full servers software development life cycles from requirement gathering, architecture discussions for the implementation, deployment, and even the production support. In my recent roles, I have focused mainly on the backend and also the cloud-based systems designing, RESTful APIs, improving the application, application performance, and the, you know, the modernization legacy applications into the microservices-oriented architectures. So I have been worked extensively with the Azure services, Docker, CI/CD pipelines, and also the automated testing to improve the reliability and also the deployment speed. Well, like what aligns with this role well with mine is not just a technical stack, but also as a leadership aspect. I have mentioned just, you know, the junior developers participated in the code reviews, collaborated closely with the, you know, the product and also the DevOps team and helped driving engineering best practices around the clean architecture, maintainability, and scalability. I''m especially interested in this opportunity because it seems to combine, you know, the hands-on engineering with ownership and also the collaboration, which, you know, where I can consistently deliver the most value.', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 2, null), ('cmox5g1bk00bdn20kjulvfymf', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that overview. Now, let’s dive into some specifics. Can you walk me through a recent project where you designed or migrated to a microservices architecture? What challenges did you face, and how did you address them?', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 3, null), ('cmox5g1bk00ben20k31da9lfr', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, well, when it comes to the design, you know, the migrated microservices architecture, the original system had come a difficulty to scale and maintain. So a single deployment impact for the, you know, the entire application, the release cycles were slow and the performance was bottleneck in one of the module affected, you know, unrelated functionality. So the goal is here is to improve the scalability, deployment independence, and the overall the system relevance. So I was the one of the senior developers responsible for the architecture and the migration strategies. So we started by identifying the bounded context within the, you know, the monolithic things like customer management and the order processing and the inventory notifications and also the balance. So from there, we gradually extracted those domains into, you know, the independent ASP.NET core microservices. Technically, the stack included having ASP.NET Core Web APIs, .NET 6, Azure Kubernetes services, and also the Azure services, Azure Service Bus for asynchronous messaging, and also SQL Server and Cosmo DB depending on the service needed, and also Docker for containerization and Azure DevOps for CI/CD pipeline. So in this, one of the key challenges that I was handling is like, you know, the communication between the services while avoiding the tight coupling. For synchronization operations, like we use the REST APIs, but for the workflows, like, you know, the order fulfillment or even the notifications, we implemented the event driving, you know, the communication throughout the Azure Service Bus. That helped mainly to improve the resilience and also reduce the direct service dependencies.', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 4, null), ('cmox5g1bk00bfn20kaqv7zonn', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I see, thanks for that detail. How did you handle any performance issues that arose during this migration to microservices?', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 5, null), ('cmox5g1bk00bgn20k7hogdgnn', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Well, when it comes to the challenges, like the performance issues for the microservices, I can say like the performance was one of the biggest areas that was, you know, worked closely during the migration because the microservices can solve some of the scaling problems, but also introduce the new latency through the network calls. So in the recent days, I have, you know, first established the baselines before the migration, which responds to the times, database query duration throughout the memory usage, and also the error rates. So that gives us the rate, something like, you know, concrete to compare against each end, each services was extracted. So one issue I can say is like, you know, running into some excessive synchronous services to the service calls. Some of the workflows became, you know, the slower because one request was waiting for the multiple downstreams APIs. So to fix this issue, you know, we moved into a non-critical steps, asynchronous processing using Azure Service Bus. For example, you know, after, like taking an order was placed, you know, the notifications or even the audit loggings and also the downstream fulfillment events, you know, were all handled by the asynchronous instead of blocking the user request. And I can say like another major area is the database performance. Like as we split the services and we reviewed the indexes, query plans, and also the, you know, the data access patterns. So in a few of the cases, we optimized the EF core queries by avoiding the unnecessary, you know, eager loadings and also using the projection instead of pulling just, you know, the full entities and adding the caches and also for the frequently accessed references data.', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 6, null), ('cmox5g1bk00bhn20kq19f2wz6', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, that makes sense. Now, could you share how you’ve applied Angular in the front-end for any of these projects?', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 7, null), ('cmox5g1bk00bin20koqjw4zh9', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, I do. Mainly for the Angular, I approached one of the front ends of one of my projects. For the microservices migration project, we had an Angular application that served as the main, you know, the user-facing portal. I worked on the features like, you know, the auto search and also the customer details and the status tracking and the dashboard views. The Angular app, which was communicated within the background through the REST APIs exposed by our.NET services, usually through the APIs gateway layer. So from an implementation standard point, I focused on building the reusable components, organizing the functionality into feature modules, and also keeping the shared UI elements in a common module. So we used the Angular services to handle the API communication and also our RxJS asynchronous data streams and also the reactive forms for complex validation scenarios. So the performance was also the important on Angular side. So we used the lazy loading for larger modules and also the paging for the large data grids. On the client side, you know, the caching was the one of the reference data that did not even change often. So I also paid some attention for avoiding unnecessary subscriptions and also used some proper, you know, unsubscribe patterns to prevent the memory leaks.', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 8, null), ('cmox5g1bk00bjn20kjbc5b6f3', 'cmox52b4h00b8n20kzbt5620w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that. Now, how did you ensure a smooth integration between your Angular front-end and the .NET back-end services?', '2026-05-08 16:48:36.272', 9, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cdn20kz4vrs46e', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 0, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cen20kxuqh0g65', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello, Jojy. Thank you for joining the interview today. Let’s get started. Could you tell me a bit about your background and', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 1, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cfn20k7bnesi91', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, can you hear me?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 2, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cgn20kv60xloex', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Yes, I can hear you loud and clear. Please go ahead and tell me about your background and how it maps to this .NET Developer role.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 3, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00chn20k587hvk07', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay. How are you?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 4, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cin20khp0lrvz6', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I''m doing well, thank you. Let''s dive in. Can you tell me a bit about your background and how it maps to this .NET Developer role?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 5, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cjn20kejeogd60', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, well, I have over 17 years of experience in developing applications using Microsoft technologies.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 6, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00ckn20kw6a6izaw', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'So last 12 years, I was working with the Wistra Energy, developing their retail applications for energy industry. I used C-sharp, developing Kubernetes APIs, and SQL for database purpose. For this requirement, I noticed that it''s a back-end developer. I do have the experience developing applications, migrating monolithic applications to Kubernetes, C-sharp, Kubernetes APIs. That''s my experience for this particular role.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 7, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cln20k3g5ukzjy', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Thanks for sharing that. Let’s go a bit deeper. How much hands-on experience do you have specifically with .NET Core and RESTful APIs?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 8, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cmn20ktg0ufzz5', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'More than five years experience I have developing. My experience is, I was with this company more than 12 years. We started with C Sharp, ASP.NET C Sharp, then moved to the WCF applications, and then migrated everything to Kubernetes service. So those changes, I was also part of the team for that. So initially we started with C Sharp .NET 4.8, then migrated to .NET Core, .NET Core 6.8 versions.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 9, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cnn20kzowdnfqh', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. And how comfortable are you with Angular for front-end development, especially versions 7 and above?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 10, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00con20kmdwuf5mu', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, front-end development, it''s like my role is 80% on the back-end and 20% on the front-end. If I can develop or modify the applications to make any Angular, any changes to the Angular front-end, it''s like a 20% role.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 11, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cpn20kzpgtdedh', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now tell me, how comfortable are you working with microservices architecture and deploying to Azure cloud?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 12, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cqn20kc70hqlmt', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes. Yeah, that is my major expertise. Like I said, 80% of my role in my previous job was developing APIs using C Sharp. That is Microsoft WISes for the products, and I was a part of the product centric team, so my role was to develop the APIs.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 13, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00crn20kha3ixh2t', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for clarifying. And how about your hands-on experience with Angular specifically?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 14, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00csn20kurbeof1d', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'That is only I can modify or add new enhancements to these existing applications. I don''t have much experience for, let''s say, building a new application using Angular. I don''t have that experience, but I have experience maintaining or adding new functionalities to an existing application.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 15, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00ctn20kiulye48c', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Thanks for that clarity. One last question—what''s your experience leading teams or mentoring junior developers?', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 16, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cun20kwf06hgnj', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, I was an SME for the area of business in my previous job. So I was taking leadership for that and mentoring developers. I was with the company, like I said, I was with the company for more than 12 years. So I was having the expertise leading the team. I was a lead developer and SME for a few applications with the company. So I was for a few new employees or new developers joining, I was training them.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 17, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cvn20k03ee3s2k', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that. That gives a solid picture. I think we’ve covered the key areas. Jojy, I appreciate your time today—we''ll be in touch soon. Thank you and take care.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 18, null), ('cmoyjuxjp00cwn20kl6o9h8ro', 'cmox7l1ym00bpn20ke6ekwity', 'CANDIDATE', 'Thank you. Bye.', '2026-05-09 16:19:52.021', 19, null), ('cmp4io1pt00din20koot1mk1f', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hi, can you hear me? Hello? Hello?', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 0, null), ('cmp4io1pt00djn20k809wuxc2', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Punith, I can hear you clearly. Thanks for joining. Let''s get started. I''m going to ask you a few questions about your background and experience. First, can you tell me a bit about your background and how it maps to this role?', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 1, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dkn20kp1k4jcq4', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, my name is Puneet, and I am a Senior Data Engineer with AI and ML experience working with Generative AIs. And I have worked over like a decade of experience handling building large-scale data systems on AI-enabled data platforms across financial, healthcare, and retail sectors. My most recent client is with SMBC Mitsubishi Corporation Banking, where I have worked in designing cloud-native data pipelines, processing more than over 4 terabytes of data daily using AWS Glue, Snowflake, and Step Functions. And I have also been familiar with MuleSoft as well as along with the working procedures and architecture of the process. Alongside the traditional data engineering, I have been heavily involved in building AI-driven systems using AWS Bedrock and LangChain, and as well as including controversial and conventional data interfaces as well, where I automate decision pipelines. And I also specialize in building both batch and as well as real-time data pipelines, implementing strong data pipeline and data quality frameworks using the great expectations and designing scalable, designing the scalable architectures that supports, you know, the downstream architecture using APIs and as well as AI use cases. My most recent focus shifted towards generative AI frameworks in AI systems, building workflows, and as well as LLMs, where I interacted with structured data, APIs, and orchestrated layers to automate the complex business procedures. And I''m particularly interested in this role because the data engineering experiences along with my generative AI skills that I''ve been developing and working on designing systems, which exactly suits my specific field of interest where I can work and focus my work on my passion towards generative AI and my interest towards creating generative AI systems that I believe where my focus relies on in future. So I am pretty much sure this aligns with the current position of the AI and ML data engineer position that is offering by the organization.', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 2, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dln20k9aocpv8f', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood, thanks for that overview. Let me dive in a bit more. Could you share some details about your experience with building ETL pipelines, particularly using Informatica or similar tools?', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 3, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dmn20klbhu33oy', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, I have built an auto-scaling computer using the ETL pipelines where I''ve used with Snowflake databases extensively on data warehouse layers in architectures, keeping things like data modeling using dimensions and data vault approaches, query optimizations using clusters and partitionings, integrations with databases from transformations, and also used secure data sharing and as well as role-based access. I have heavily worked on Snowflake in the backend and used AI use cases where I structured the data using the query dynamics, using the LLM generated, sorry.', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 4, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dnn20kkunsgolw', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'CANDIDATE', 'As SQLs and as well as coming to the ETL pipelines, I have used Airflow orchestrations for ETL pipelines using the DAGs for dependency management retries and as well as rescheduling. In AWS environment, I mostly focused, used on step functions as serverless alternatives, especially for the event-driven workflows, and as well as I am comfortable with the Airflow and cloud-native orchestration patterns as well.', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 5, null), ('cmp4io1pt00don20kbwdvvc1k', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How comfortable are you working with Salesforce platforms and data models, and what specific projects have you handled there?', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 6, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dpn20kyothbgj2', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'CANDIDATE', 'So coming to the Salesforce platforms, I have worked with CRM integrations, data pipelines, where we ingest and process customer data and transform the data that fed downstream systems, including the CRM platforms. You can say while I haven''t directly worked with Salesforce native environment, but components like Apex, I have worked with API-based integration and data pipelines that supported the CRM workflows. For the MuleSoft, I''ve integrated and implemented the API orchestrations using pipeline servers, like using the Python for that and AWS Lambda in one of the projects where I''ve used it for integrating the MuleSoft with AWS servers, which serves a similar purpose in connecting the systems. So this, which was one of my recent clients in healthcare, that''s Evelyn''s Health, that I''ve extensively worked on with MuleSoft integrations with their cloud native platforms like AWS and as well as the Azure platforms, and that supported the CRM workflows.', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 7, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dqn20kcen4fvto', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How would you rate your proficiency in writing complex Python modules for custom ETL workflows?', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 8, null), ('cmp4io1pt00drn20k6wtfrps3', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I''ve used extensively PySpark and Pandas for the ETL pipelines and as well as the Flask and Lambda for the API developments. And I''m also familiar with Bedrock and Landshun LLM integrations where I worked extensively for the past six years on the LLM integrations and workflow automations. I pretty much say I have built modular Python services that access the intermediates between the LLMs and as well as the structured data systems. I can say I''m pretty much familiar. I can rate myself around somewhere where an experienced professional can integrate and as well as orchestrate the design and architecture position. And I''m pretty much with my experience and expertise in the data engineering, traditional data engineering techniques and automation techniques that I have been using for the past few years. And I''m pretty much, I''m pretty much like more than an intermediate level in the Python and as well as AI integration using Python. I''m pretty much I can go for myself as advanced engineer where I can integrate and automate the LLMs.', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 9, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dsn20kp7ihu5b0', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for clarifying. Now, how have you incorporated LangChain or similar agentic frameworks in your recent work?', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 10, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dtn20kleoy6xmc', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'CANDIDATE', 'So LangChain, I''ve used it for, you can say, for the pipelines where I''ve orchestrated agentic AI''s, uh, early stages, uh, agentic workflows, primarily using AWS Bedrocks and as well as uh LangChains. For instance, I''ve built a conversational interface where financial users uh from like SMBC could query uh portfolio data using the natural language uh under under the hood. Uh you can say it was like, it just not uh wasn''t a prompting response, but I have built multi-step workflows for that, which uses uh user queries, where passed uh phrased using the LLMs and as well as mapped into the structured SQL queries on Snowflake and parallelly executing via APIs as well, resulting in enriched and returned with a context. So I have implemented this orchestration using the step functions uh to stimulate the agent like behavior, break down the tasks into smaller steps like query generation, validation, execution, and after that summarization, while I have maintained uh it by mainly using LangChain and I''m currently uh exploring more advanced frameworks uh like LangGraph and better statement management in multi-step uh agentic workflows.', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 11, null), ('cmp4io1pt00dun20ka6htuwby', 'cmp4i8u1400dgn20ktsium0t7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks. One last question before we wrap up: could you briefly describe your experience with vector databases and how you''ve applied them in RAG pipelines?', '2026-05-13 20:33:08.274', 12, null), ('cmp4k91ua00een20kzdb7k3y2', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Pratyusha, thanks for joining today. I’m going to guide you through this interview for the Software Engineer role. Let’s get started with a quick introduction. Could you tell me a bit about your background and how it aligns with this role?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 0, null), ('cmp4k91ua00efn20kvqe9fj6l', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, sure. So I''m a senior full-stack Java developer with over 11 years of experience in designing, developing, and building some scalable enterprise applications using Java, Spring Boot, microservices, and RESTful APIs development. My recent work at Cigna has been focused on developing some Spring Boot microservices, event-driven systems with Apache Kafka, and integrating LLM and like a workflow and pre-trained models into enterprise applications. So before that, at City and MetLife, I worked on high-volume distributed systems, cloud-native deployments, and intelligent like search solutions using the Elasticsearch, Docker, Kubernetes, and AWS, or GPS cloud platforms I used with this. What aligns well with this is my hands-on experience in Java backend architecture, AI and ML integration, like even during the designs and building secure production-grade services in like agile environments. I also completed my master''s in information systems from the University of Memphis, which further strengthened my understanding on modern enterprise systems and data-driven application designs. Overall, my background is strongly aligned with this role because it combines core Java backend expertise with microservices, cloud, and AI and ML enterprise application development.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 1, null), ('cmp4k91ua00egn20k6b0o1f54', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that overview. Let’s dive a bit deeper into your experience with microservices. Can you walk me through a specific project where you designed and developed a set of microservices using Java and Spring Boot?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 2, null), ('cmp4k91ua00ehn20kg65sjgcj', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, yeah, sure. Like I have done like in current project I worked on healthcare platform where I designed and developed some SpringBoot-based microservices for a provider and claims-related workflows. My responsibility was to break a monolithic flow into a smaller services such as member data, claim processing, and providing the provider onboarding and expose them through RESTful APIs endpoints while using some Apache Kafka for real-time event streaming. And also I, like I used some Spring Cloud for service-to-service communication, Docker for containerization, and Kubernetes for AWS and for the Elastic Kubernetes service for deployment and scaling. I also implement security using OAuth2 and JSON Web Token for the secure API access and like leverage Elastic Search for interactive search capabilities on onboarding models. One good example was improving some claim lookup and provider''s workflow performance, like by what is by moving some legacy modules to microservices and optimizing the high-volume data access with MongoDB. So this helps like improve scalability deployment in like independence and also response time. So overall this project gave me strong hands-on experience in like design, secure, scalable, event-driven microservices using the Java and the Spring Boot in a production environment.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 3, null), ('cmp4k91ua00ein20kmccnwl1y', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, that’s helpful. How did you handle monitoring and troubleshooting these microservices in production?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 4, null), ('cmp4k91ua00ejn20kakbyryoc', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I have done like in production, we use uh uh what is that? We use some uh monitoring and troubleshooting at multiple levels at Cigna was doing both microservices were like uh uh contact with the Docker and deployed in Kubernetes in the AWS. So I use the centralized logging Kubernetes uh all level checks and uh API level monitoring to quickly identify some failure like services. Like uh for troubleshooting, I typically start with application logs, so like a uh break off from message flow validations and development level checks to isolate like whether the issue is from the service, uh event pipeline or uh infrastructures. So since I also worked on uh ServiceNow uh ITSM and uh like uh CMDB, so integrated workflows like this incident tracking and root cause like a a follow-up were a part of uh part of the operational process as well. So one example was when I response time increased for uh like a uh claim lookup APIs and I analyzed MongoDB with query like a performance and optimized the data access layer, which like improved the API response time. So my approach is to combine proactive monitoring, log analysis, and uh infrastructure checks and performance tuning to keep uh like uh microservices stable in production.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 5, null), ('cmp4k91ua00ekn20kgtue1m56', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you handle scaling those microservices when traffic spiked?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 6, null), ('cmp4k91ua00eln20kxgsel0bk', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'So when I handled scaling mainly through container-based environment like a stateless service design and even during architecture. And at Cigna, I was doing both microservices were like deployed on a Kubernetes in AWS. So we scaled our services horizontally by like increasing some more pod replies based on like traffic and workload patterns. Also, we made sure these services were like loosely coupled and stateless, which helped us scale individual components like independently without affecting the full systems. For asynchronous high volume flows, I used Apache Kafka or also traffic spikes could be absorbed through messaging instead of overloading the APIs directly. So example was during high claim processing volume where we like what we say, we scale only the claim and member-related services while keeping some other services unchained. So like we also optimize MongoDB query and caching where needed to reduce backend pressure. So overall, my approach was to combine Kubernetes-based horizontal scaling, Kafka-driven asynchronous processing, and database optimizations to handle traffic growth efficiently.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 7, null), ('cmp4k91ua00emn20kpx6su7ns', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Makes sense, thanks for explaining that. Let’s shift gears—can you describe your experience with Neo4j and graph-based systems?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 8, null), ('cmp4k91ua00enn20kyyh2ez6l', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'Definitely. So Neo4j, I have like worked in a style example data models and a graph-based systems, mainly in the context of semantic data traversal, knowledge graph patterns, and also graph RAG, like a graph-type style, like architecture has reflected in my resume. So in my current role at Cigna, I, like I built some knowledge graph style data models using like a graphQL to represent relationship across provider and claims data, which help support semantic traversal and intelligent driven use cases. My experience is more on the application and integration side where I used a graph modeling concept to design connected enterprise data structures like rather like rather than working only with the flat relational models. So I also have hands-on from that with Neo4j graph data modeling, semantic search, and graph RAG patterns as part of like a AI-driven architecture, like integrated with the Java microservices. So overall, my experience with the graph-based systems is centered on modeling relationships, enabling semantic search, and supporting AI-powered enterprise workflows.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 9, null), ('cmp4k91ua00eon20kezeyo14t', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that. One last question: how comfortable are you integrating large language models with these graph-based systems in a production', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 10, null), ('cmp4k91ua00epn20kkpolr66p', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'Thanks for that.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 11, null), ('cmp4k91ua00eqn20kk38hdk28', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Thanks, Pratyusha. I appreciate your time today, and we’ll be in touch with', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 12, null), ('cmp4k91ua00ern20kwj3xq6iq', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', '마비쳐야 돼.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 13, null), ('cmp4k91ua00esn20ktd2xhpip', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'You’re welcome. Best of luck, and have a great rest of your day. Take care.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 14, null), ('cmp4k91ua00etn20k2o5gpodm', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'You''re welcome.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 15, null), ('cmp4k91ua00eun20kbu1f8beb', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'How comfortable are you integrating large language models with these graph-based systems in a production environment?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 16, null), ('cmp4k91ua00evn20kwazmw6bf', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'How comfortable are you? Can you repeat?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 17, null), ('cmp4k91ua00ewn20k1cymzkay', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Sure. How comfortable are you integrating large language models with these graph-based systems', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 18, null), ('cmp4k91ua00exn20kgwzcik3k', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'En idior.', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 19, null), ('cmp4k91ua00eyn20kpbgx7xso', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'CANDIDATE', 'Can you repeat the question, please?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 20, null), ('cmp4k91ua00ezn20kovxdaylw', 'cmp4jvh4000ecn20kdvvh1a4a', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Of course. How comfortable are you integrating large language models with these graph-based systems in a production environment?', '2026-05-13 21:17:27.827', 21, null), ('cmp4l2en600fan20kyi5ldeq5', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'CANDIDATE', 'Say hi.', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 0, null), ('cmp4l2en600fbn20kqd2z4c4h', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello, Naveen. This is your interview for the Senior Data Engineer, AI/ML role. Let’s get started. Can you tell me a bit about your background and how it maps to this position?', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 1, null), ('cmp4l2en600fcn20k8ats7dw6', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks, Naveen. That’s a solid overview. Let’s go deeper. Can you describe a recent project where you implemented agentic workflows with LangGraph and what challenges you faced?', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 2, null), ('cmp4l2en600fdn20kapcizov6', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, you know, my name is Naveen and I''m a senior data engineer, you know, working more than 12 years. So coming to my expertise, you know, I''ve been dealing with the agentic capabilities, placing something working at the Home Depot because we are building the system where we do have the agents that automatically, you know, adds the supply data onboarding because they need their documentation, map fields, and generate the transformation logic as well. And even they will create the DBT models. So I''ve been using the language graph with multiple special agents. So we''ll be collaborating with different teams, right? So because, you know, one handles the schema analysis and the other does the mapping logic. And the third one will do the automatic output. So basically on the data engineering fundamentals, I, you know, whole stack, mainly like Informatica for ETL, where I''ve been using in my previous client as well. So and I do use Airflow as well for orchestration. And the warehouse is like Snowflake. And I''m using TensorFlow Python as well, mainly for the custom transformation logic. And before client, I used to work on real-time pipelines as well, dealing on the transactional data, maybe like 15 to 20 DPS during the certain peekers. So I''m very pretty comfortable with, you know, batch and streaming as well. So the Salesforce integration, it''s kind of interesting part because I''m not working directly with Salesforce CRM. I''ve built the bidirectional sync pipelines between the certain systems. At my current client, we do also have the vendor performance data, which is going to in our system using the MuleSoft. So the concepts of, you know, adding the data, adding the APIs as well, this will be giving you a familiar territory. And I''m some LLM and vector database. I do have the certain experience as well by building rack pipelines using the Pinecone. And I''ve been working with OpenAI as well and Anthropic APIs. This will be giving the, you know, prompt engineering behind the demos. Yeah, this is all pretty basic introvert.', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 3, null), ('cmp4l2en600fen20kz4dc50an', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you ensure the data quality and consistency across those agent handoffs?', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 4, null), ('cmp4l2en600ffn20kun85jn1k', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'CANDIDATE', 'Got you. So coming to this scenario, I''ve been working with different projects like the supplier onboarding automation that is with our current client. So the problem was, you know, we have the massive backlog where the new suppliers will send the product catalog files. So our team, you know, will spend many days manually figuring out what the schema is and writing the mapping rules here and building the ETL jobs. And we are getting, you know, maybe like 30 to 20 new suppliers, maybe like around like maybe three to five days, this will be going to be onboard. So I''m building a multi-agent system as well using Langrave, where we''ll be having the four main agents within a certain graph. First is the layer agent that reads the supplier files, which might be CSV or Excel, and it will generate a schema understanding as well. So then in terms of the mapping agent, this will come, you know, compare the product taxonomy within our Snowflake database. And the third thing was the validation agent. This will be checking the mappings if they are running with some sample transformations. And finally, a code generation agent, that''s kind of DBT model and also the conversion with the Airflow decks. So this is the biggest challenge was like the state management between the different agents because you know, each agent gets messier because that needs like the parsing as well and also different objects, maybe in terms of the SQL queries. So I ended up using a combination of Pythonic models, this structure and stored the air facts mainly in our S3 within the references of the state graph. The other point was the rendering and retrace because some MLMs, you know, they don''t have the generated invalid sequence. So I need to give you feedback as well where the validation needs to be generated within the certain graph. So I''ll be using, you know, different GPT models as well, like 4, 3.5 version where we''ll be having 800 to 1000 tokens mainly on the supplier files.', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 5, null), ('cmp4l2en600fgn20kcy7joqyv', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How did you handle the integration with Snowflake for those transformations?', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 6, null), ('cmp4l2en600fhn20kixq9dd4f', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, you know, in terms of the data quality and the handoff validation, this kind of critical, you know, because one output from an early agent would cascade the whole workflow. So how do we implement a few layers here? First thing is for the schema contracts between the certain agents, because each agent has to be pulling out the output data in a pipeline model. And the next agent would be validating the structure before, you know, doing anything. And I''ve been analyzing the written and fields as well by doing some, you know, valid and validations. Second was the checkpointing with the human review. For the few months, you know, we didn''t run the full load and miss versions. So each major agent gets the output in terms of the staging table within a certain vehicles. So we''ll be using the flag like from the reviews. And mainly our data engineers, you know, will be spotting like 20% of the outputs. This actually building some validation data sets so that, you know, when the agent gets something wrong, we''ll be logging that with certain example and few-shot prompting as well. So validation isn''t this kind of itself, you know, in terms of role-based checks, mainly on the LLM reasoning. Things like map day filters, you know, we add this mainly to our confidence scores. So that each agent will run not the results, but the confidence level. And if the mapping agent is the able like 0.7 confidence, I''ll be routing a different node within a langref so that, you know, it will be giving a different approach for a human review. So this finally kept the false positive rate manageable and we are simply catching about like 90% of the issues before the production.', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 7, null), ('cmp4l2en600fin20k2thsj819', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'CANDIDATE', 'Here you know when we talk about the integration in terms of the Snowflake, I do have the two parts. One is the runtime validation piece, and the other thing is the generated pipeline deployment. So for the runtime validations, I will be validating the agent. You know, that''s needs to be tested the proceed mappings. So in terms of the Snowflake, I will be using the Python connector to spin up the temporary tables. We will be having the supply raw files as well. That''s going to land in our Snowflake stage. So we''ll be having, you know, different kinds of stages across the 500 rows, mainly on the isolated schema. And mainly for the production, we''ll be having the compute cost as well. That trigger part was we''ll be managing the Snowflake sessions, mainly with, you know, the agent workflows because that was creating a new connection for a particular agent task and it was pretty slow hitting some connection limits. So I switched simply using a connection pool platform where I''ll be using the lang graph mainly to work on the Snowflake sessions. And I''ll be checking out the connections as well if they are needed. And I''ll be very careful with the transaction isolation as well because that will be giving the validation run across the different rollbacks. And in terms of the DBT deployment, the code generation agent simply, you know, write the DBT files mainly to our Git repository. And I''ll be running the issues as well in Snowflake warehouse sizing. The agent, you know, these will be querying in terms of the optimization. They will be running with our small warehouse and the timeouts as well, so that I will simply add the logic to the code generation. That will be giving the best practices in terms of logic data sets.', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 8, null), ('cmp4l2en600fjn20k3igh93cj', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'INTERVIEWER', 'That makes sense. How did you optimize the Snowflake warehouse sizing during high-volume loads?', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 9, null), ('cmp4l2en600fkn20k541h6e07', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, now in terms of high volume loads, I would say like we do follow a demand dynamic warehouse sizing. This kind of strategy because I''ll be implementing the airflow sensor. This will be checking the incoming file size and the raw count as well before kicking off in the snowflake processing. So I will be dealing under like 10 million rows, mainly in terms of the XML warehouse. Anything above like smaller medium, we do have like four to five different warehouses based on the sizes. And you know, we do use like DAG mainly as well. So I''ll be giving the auto assessment. This will be kind of settings so that you know the agents workflows, this can be intermittent, maybe like 15 to 20 on boardings per week. So we didn''t like like warehouses, you know, running 24 by seven. So I do configure the warehouses for a two minutes of inactivity in terms of auto assessment. Mainly in terms of large loads, I would say like we''ll be using multi-cluster warehouses. I''ll be setting out a warehouse to scale, you know, one to three clusters during the certain bakers. If there are more than two queries, right, we''ll be setting up then the cluster as well, because that will be giving you the period where we''ll be running the validation test team intensely. And one thing was the original caching, that''s kind of validation agent because, you know, that will be running the same test query like different multiple times. So which was like completely wasteful. So I''ll be adding a logic to check the snowflake history based on the information cached scheme and information we are getting from the queries. So I, you know, results are getting spinned up as well based on the compute.', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 10, null), ('cmp4l2en600fln20k8ppr19ho', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that. Final question: why are you interested in this role, and what excites you most about it?', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 11, null), ('cmp4l2en600fmn20ke7tj4ccj', 'cmp4koj6g00f5n20ks7q0pb4d', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, you know, in terms of my interest, so these roles like give me like more depth into, you know, AI ML engineering concepts. So I''ll be preferring, you know, that''s my current trend where I''ll be dealing large amount of AI models and other stuff. So I''ll be doing, you know, implement the new models and predict the outcomes as well. So based on, you know, working with different techs like Snowflake, Apache Dax, you know, land graphs as well, that will be helpful for me in terms of the, you know, from one on that stuff.', '2026-05-13 21:40:17.443', 12, null), ('cmp4l3emj00fpn20k0vj212cu', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Is...', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 0, null), ('cmp4l3emj00fqn20k8qxsrzww', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello, Marru. Thank you for joining the interview today. I’m going to walk you through a few questions to understand your background and technical expertise for this Software Engineer role. Let’s start with a brief introduction—can you tell me a bit about your background and how it maps to this role?', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 1, null), ('cmp4l3emj00frn20k7b728g2o', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, sure. Absolutely. I''ve been working as a job full stack developer for eight years now. I''ve worked across like, you know, different industries like finance, telecom, retail, which has been like a pretty broad like a perspective on how to build like scalable, reliable systems in different contexts. So right now I''m working at Comcast in Philly, where I''m working since like October 2025. And I have been like working as a cloud native applications using Java 11, Python 3, and Spring Boot, microservices, all running on AWS. And we are dealing with like a pretty high volume distributed system. So a lot of the focus is on like event-driven architecture with Kafka, AWS, Lambdas, and DynamoDB and like step functions, basically making like sure like everything are scalable and reliable. And also been working doing a lot of with the observability, like integrating with Slack, tech stack like a ELK for centralized logging and Grafana for monitoring. And honestly, that has been a huge for reducing our mean time to resolution with incidents happen. Before that, I worked with TD Bank in New Jersey for like around like an year for the financial services. That was working with integrating Kafka, synchronous processing, working with AWS, Node.js for backend, for the front end, for React, and security and compliance with OAuth 2.0, Spring security. Everything was looked down properly. And before that, I have been working with Wind Supply in Ohio and before like I assume worked with AA and Connecticab where I worked as an insurance applications. And I also done like masters in computer science from Marist College in New York, which I was finished in 2023 and was working in like India at like Eval solutions for about four and a half years, like code, Java development, Spring boot framework. And you are looking for someone with like a strong backend with Java and spring boot microservices and the AI, ML integration is a piece of interesting to me because I''ve been working with Comcast like integrated OpenAI LLM APIs for like a log summarization and incident rise. And I built like an internal RAG-based application during hackathon like using fast API and quadrant and Olama. So that idea of bringing like AI into enterprise Java applications is something I genuinely excited about. You know, I''ve been working with AWS like extensively, EC2, Lambda and S3 and cloud formation. And yeah, I think my background is distributed systems, microservices, cloud infrastructure, and I''m also like AI, ML exposure would be pretty good fit for this what I''m looking for.', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 2, null), ('cmp4l3emj00fsn20kw42nsvyq', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that overview. Let’s dig a bit deeper. Can you walk me through your experience designing and developing RESTful APIs and microservices, particularly in a distributed architecture context?', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 3, null), ('cmp4l3emj00ftn20k5riazlh1', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How did you handle scaling those microservices under heavy load?', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 4, null), ('cmp4l3emj00fun20kj9ij4h4v', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, sure. Coming to that, I''ve been working with RESTful APIs and microservices pretty much throughout my career, but I would say the most intensive experience that was been like at Comcast and TD Bank where we are dealing with like a highly like a high volume distributed systems. So at Comcast, we are building like cloud native applications with Spring Boot, microservices, and running on AWS and like architecture is like fully distributed. So I have the services communicating via REST APIs and also event-driven patterns with like a Kafka and AWS Lambda. And one thing I have been worked was like designing RESTful APIs for, you know, like backend services that handle like a customer data workflows. And we have like made sure this API is where like scalable and reliable because we are talking about millions of requests per day, right? So I''m designing a RESTful API always starts with like a resource model that are like entities with operations to need and I follow RESTful principles pretty strictly, get for reads, post for creates, put for updates, deletes for deletes and proper HTTP codes, you know, like 200 for success, 400 for not found, 500 for server errors. At Comcast, I also implemented standard exceptional handling across our microservices because before it kind of inconsistent and debugging was nightmare. So now every service returns like a consistent error response structure with error codes, message and correlation ID for tracing. And GraphQL actually for like some of these use cases, which let like client requests exactly filled I needed like a query instead of multiple REST calls and the page load like improved noticeably in terms of distributed architecture. One of the big things I''ve been learned and Is that like just you cannot just treat microservices like a monolith. You have like a service discovery and distributed tracing and centralized logging at the infrastructure. At the Comcast, I set up like end to end like request correlations using Java MDC and Python structured logging. So every request like a unique correlation ID which flows through the services and we can track by using like ELK stack dashboards that has been a huge for troubleshooting production issues. You can exactly know which request failed and which downstream services like called like and it also worked with event driven patterns. Like at Comcast, we use like Kafka heavily for like asynchronous processing and these have been like services we can consume and do their own processing.', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 5, null), ('cmp4l3emj00fvn20kkzfw383j', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, coming to that like for the heavy load, I''ve been dealt with like a lot, especially at Comcast and TD where like, you know, we are handling like really high volumes of traffic. So at Comcast, we are running our microservices on AWS, AKS, and with Kubernetes on AWS, and I configured like a horizontal pod autoscalers, which basically monitors like a CPU and memory metrics and automatically scale the number of pooled replicas up or down based on the thresholds. I said, so for example, if average CPU usage across like 70%, like the HPA would like a HPA would sign up more parts to handle the load. And when it is dropped below like 30%, it will scale back down. This was like a really important because some of the services handle millions of requests per day. And like traffic patterns are like constant, like, you know, getting strikes during peak hours, and then it drops off night. And so you don''t want to uh paying for like peak capacity 24 by 7. So we also implemented like a rolling update strategies like in Kubernetes, so we could like deploy new versions with zero downtime instead of like taking the whole service down. So Kubernetes gradually replaces like old posts with new ones and if something goes down, it it can roll back automatically. That''s been like huge for maintaining availability during deployments.', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 6, null), ('cmp4l3emj00fwn20kpjegvvna', 'cmp4kpht600f8n20keniss8gf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How have you incorporated Neo4j or other graph technologies in your recent work?', '2026-05-13 21:41:04.075', 7, null), ('cmp4ny13h00g4n20kghlp6gl7', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'CANDIDATE', 'I can''t hear you. Can you please repeat?', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 0, null), ('cmp4ny13h00g5n20kno1082q5', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Yes, I can hear you clearly. Let’s begin. Hi Rakesh, I’m glad you’re here. I’m going to walk us through a short interview for the Data Engineer - AI/ML role. Let’s start with a bit about your background and how it maps to this role.', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 1, null), ('cmp4ny13h00g6n20kj6ntxv8v', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'CANDIDATE', 'I started off with my master''s in machine learning and I''ve been working as a data engineer, as an AI engineer for almost like 10 plus years in the IT industry. And during this experience, I have extensively worked on setting up the building of the ETL pipelines from scratch and identifying the data models, working with the stakeholders of the product team, and also working with various team members such as data scientists, data analysts, or in case of this like cross-application team members as well. And while doing so, I was able to work on various tools on warehouses such as like Snowflake, GCP, AWS, and all. And my programming expertise relies on specifically on Python and Java. And I have like very, I would consider myself as an expert in SQL. And in my recent projects, I have like extensively utilized different AI or like LLM models in our project to optimize a few approaches like that we are considering in our current pipelines and also working or utilizing these same models and models to extensively enhance the golden data set that we are trying to prepare.', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 2, null), ('cmp4ny13h00g7n20kp25g6pqd', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks, Rakesh. That gives a good starting point. Now, can you tell me about a specific example where you built a complex ETL pipeline from scratch using Python and Snowflake?', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 3, null), ('cmp4ny13h00g8n20kgwraf5d9', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. That’s a detailed walkthrough. How did you handle any performance optimizations in that pipeline?', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 4, null), ('cmp4ny13h00g9n20k88dsaxv9', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure. So as I explained, right, I have used Python in Snowflake across my career. And Python is like I have used in multiple stages. So to talk about statistically, how do we set up an ETL pipeline with Python in Snowflake here is, so firstly, I will try to identify the sources that are application source teams, which are managing the ETL pipeline. And I would identify what are the list of sources and I will create a data model out of each table and then have these source team respective tables, which will be considered as a raw layer, which will be pulled in using the Python scripts. For example, if it is a ODBC connection Oracle database, we can use ODBC or any JDBC for SQL server already has a connection. And using SQLAlchemy or Pyspark copy tool. And we can connect to these databases. And we can set up these ETL triggers on these databases to identify the changes that are happening on these individual tables as well. That was old technique and the new technique we can use, it is golden gate to retrieve the CSV files or else the Postgres SQL has what do we say, the VAL archive and also SQL server has this SSIS and SSIS, which will generate these CSV files as we need as a changes. Maybe we can consume this and then land them in the Snowflake staging area. So in the Snowflake staging area, we can create this external table using Python ETL Python script excels. And again, which will execute, we can have these SQL queries that we want to create, which will do the transformation. So in the ETL pipeline, the major concentration that I would give is having the medullin architecture, which is like very optimized one using bronze, silver, gold, which can be acting as like a raw transform then and the final golden data set. So in this way, like I would set up this Python script along with the Snowflake to continuously transform the data and then filter the data as needed and by creating these multiple SQL queries and then creating these temporary tables at runtime on the Snowflake instance using Python, I will be able to do this. And for orchestration, I can utilize Airflow to execute these Python scripts on which will do the execution of the Snowflake, this ETL pipeline flow.', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 5, null), ('cmp4ny13h00gan20kqc1uk2hk', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'CANDIDATE', 'So let''s say how do we handle performance of this? So here there could be various reasons. So one, we need to understand like different kinds of joins that we are trying to do, and we need to ensure if the table is created, is it partitioned or ordered by a specific key column using like something like a cluster by column, which will ensure that the data is partitioned and if we have to do any where clauses or if we have to do any joins with another table using that column, it will be efficient join. So in this way, like we can do some optimization and on the Snowflake side, if we can do this create table, I would say while creating the pipeline, I would ensure that we can do a backtrace step, meaning we can set up the Snowflake tables in such a way that I mean like the pipeline in such a way that even if there is a failure, like we can just recreate the data again using different like the slowly changing dimension table. And with respect to optimization, those were like some techniques which I explained earlier, like joins and also the partition pruning and enhanced cluster warehousing, like the Snowflake cluster, virtual warehouse setup. In this way, we can ensure that the whole pipeline is running in an optimized way.', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 6, null), ('cmp4ny13h00gbn20koxbw64oo', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let’s move to another area. How have you worked with LLM APIs and agentic frameworks like LangChain in your recent projects?', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 7, null), ('cmp4ny13h00gcn20khux551qo', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, so coming to LLM models usage in my current work. So we had this scenario where we have the five-part code set up. We had a huge repository where we kind of a monolithic repository where we have like multiple teams contributing to it on different, let''s say, strategies. That''s what we call. And for each strategy and when the team is enhancing or the code changes, we were covering the unit test cases and we had an issue with where the coverage is getting dropped continuously day by day. So using LLM, we have introduced LLM models. We integrated a cloud in our model, I mean, in our document, like the cloud and all. And we created an environment where we will install cloud and we will provide this repository. And whenever it will, whenever the testing threshold, if it is dropping less than 80%, it will identify the biggest changes that it can bring, I mean, add the test cases to enhance it up to and then add more test cases to it. That is one way where we optimized our current flow. And in the code itself, we have utilized LLM to identify, for example, if we have any patient information, for example, if there are any null values, like what could be the probable value, for example, like some zip code, like what could be the values that we can populate and some scenarios we can identify. In this way, I have worked with like extensively with cloud to integrate using Python and Langchain. So using Langchain, we were able to establish like multiple roles for these models, which will act as one will act as the data creator and one will act as the another model will act as the data validator. In this way, whatever the data is created by LLM as in an ad hoc way also, we are just ensuring that this is created in a proper way and there is no issue going forward.', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 8, null), ('cmp4ny13h00gdn20kcle0ah8g', 'cmp4nivx500g2n20kqqslbssp', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that. Now, how did you manage integrating LangChain with your existing data pipelines?', '2026-05-13 23:00:52.109', 9, null), ('cmp6whzt70005nx0kiv3ovshc', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 0, null), ('cmp6whzt70006nx0kgd9spfh2', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello, Ashmika. My name is David, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s get started. Could you begin by telling me a bit about your background and how it maps to this Software Engineer role?', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 1, null), ('cmp6whzt70007nx0k95chz0qp', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hi David, this is Ashmika and I''ve been working in the software industry for more than 15 years now and I have worked in various domains like insurance, banking, finance.', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 2, null), ('cmp6whzt70008nx0k77glzddp', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'CANDIDATE', 'And healthcare. And also, I have done a lot of work on Java, Springboard, and other server-side technologies, along with a good amount of experience working in SQL, database, and as well as front-end technologies like React, Angular. And that''s why I think I''m a good fit for this project, plus this project also needs somebody who can mentor the other team members, along with that, also take responsibilities, multiple responsibilities. So I have already done that in a lot of my earlier projects, and that''s why I find myself fit for this.', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 3, null), ('cmp6whzt70009nx0kny81knr2', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that, Ashmika. Let’s dive a bit deeper. Can you walk me through your hands-on experience with building scalable systems using Java and Spring Boot?', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 4, null), ('cmp6whzt7000anx0kp9vby1hz', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, in order to build a scalable system using Java and Spring Boot, the most important thing is to make sure that we are interacting both the systems together and making sure that the Java and Spring Boot are both making the system much more scalable, reliable, and at the same time, making the system much more flexible so that any new component can be introduced at any point of time. So basically, I would design such a scalable system by keeping in mind the architecture should be modular, it should be stateless, also distributed architecture would be best, and like I would also concentrate on performance optimization. So the Spring Boot microservices can be exposed using REST API, that will make the system much more better in many ways. And at the application level, I will keep the services mostly stateless. That will help me in many ways, and I''ll use load balancers, and I''ll also use some kind of, like, for deployment purposes, I''ll use Docker, Kubernetes, and I''ll focus more on proper indexing of the system. At the same time, query optimization, all those things will make my system much more better. In terms of asynchronous communication, I would prefer using Kafka, RabbitMQ, or Spring batches. So that will be so helpful in making sure that the proper interaction between the components happens. For caching, I can go for using Redis in my system, and overall, I''ll build a scalable Java Spring system using microservices, and I''ll use stateless services, load balancing, caching, combination of all these and make my system much better.', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 5, null), ('cmp6whzt7000bnx0k3opq6wxa', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, thanks for that. Now, can you give me an example of a RESTful API or microservice you’ve designed and developed recently, and what challenges you faced?', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 6, null), ('cmp6whzt7000cnx0kxiiqmrm9', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, so I think, sorry, can you please continue?', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 7, null), ('cmp6whzt7000dnx0k35ltvo00', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Sure. Could you share an example of a RESTful API or microservice that you designed and developed recently?', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 8, null), ('cmp6whzt7000enx0kbzvv4x7c', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, so I developed a system. I built REST API for a claims processing system where the adjusters and the downstream systems consumed some kind of claim details. So the APIs were used for claim creation, claim status, tracking, then reservation management, then payment workflows, and I implemented validation, role-based authentication, exception handling. Also, I did pagination and optimized SQL queries for faster retrieval. So that''s how I implemented it.', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 9, null), ('cmp6whzt7000fnx0kqpkf12x6', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, thanks. How did you approach the integration of that API with downstream systems or external services?', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 10, null), ('cmp6whzt7000gnx0kmdova66r', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now, can you tell me about your experience working with Neo4j or any graph-based technologies in your projects?', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 11, null), ('cmp6whzt7000hnx0k2rmd211r', 'cmp6w29j20003nx0kycacd354', 'CANDIDATE', 'So in order to integrate that API with the downstream systems, what we have to think about is we want to make sure that if there is any error or failure, it gets tracked. So we have to take care of that as well. So I made sure that this system makes that design much more flexible in a way that this thing will be taken care of. So first of all, I understood the downstream system that I have in place. Then I also tried to understand the request and response schema that it would generate, then the authentication mechanism. Then I tried to understand the rate limits, SLA and time executions. And at the same time, I also looked at error handling logic, plus what kind of structure I would like in order to generate that. So I avoided calling the downstream APIs directly from the controllers. And this helped me to improve the maintainability and testability. At the same time, also make sure that my code is loosely coupled. And then I used like a web client for interacting with the third-party systems because a web client would make it much more faster and better compared to the REST templates. So that was one of the things that I did. And I added a at some kind of timeout handling. This helped me to slow down the downstream systems because a lot of times the downstream systems get slowed down and can cause some kind of exhaustion at the thread level. So this would make sure that our system works correctly. Also, I added a circuit breaker in my system that helped me prevent any kind of failure situation. That was one of the things that I did. And retry, like logic I implemented for timeout situations. And definitely logging and tracing is a very, very important part. Like we have to add request correlation IDs, then API latency. So all these things were implemented. And for logging and tracing, I used Splunk, which is a very important tool that I have worked on. And then error handling is also very important. So in my code, I did it using try-catch blocks. And instead of using or exposing the raw errors, I did use some global error handling system in my approach. So that was very good. And for heavy loads, if I wanted to use a stream or some kind of asynchronous communication, I made it through Kafka. In Kafka, I made sure that we are making the system much more scalable, loosely coupled, and fault tolerant. So that''s how I implemented the whole system.', '2026-05-15 12:35:52.843', 12, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000rnx0kyp6xtxoq', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 0, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000snx0kd8s0kulo', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello, can you hear me?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 1, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000tnx0kv5547bsb', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Deepak, yes I can hear you clearly.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 2, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000unx0kuw4t1y9t', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 3, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000vnx0kebwc2cvk', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Deepak, good to connect. Let’s begin. Can you start by telling me a bit about your background and how it maps to this Software Engineer role?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 4, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000wnx0ke586duqy', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, so I have an excellent, I have a good experience in the backend activities. So I have total of 16 years of experience in software development. I have been deep in background. I have a deep background in designing and scaling complex backend systems using Java and Spring Boot, which aligns directly with the requirement of a lead principal engineer.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 5, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000xnx0kqacx8fzq', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'And I have worked on the microservices architecture, and I''ve also worked on AWS and cloud environment. Yes.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 6, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000ynx0kvsdwh4hv', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, thanks for sharing. Let’s dig deeper. Can you walk me through your experience designing and developing RESTful APIs and microservices?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 7, null), ('cmp6y6v6f000znx0kgta17exf', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, for sure. So over 16 years of experience, including extensive work at PNC and Independent Health, and I focus basically on migrating the monolithic architecture into smaller springboard microservices. So in this project, I have designed multiple microservices, which include the REST microservices, IBM MQ microservices. The other microservices including Kafka, which are basically the event-driven, and we have basically deployed it in the AWS platform. And for the performance and optimization, we have included the Redis caching, and yes.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 8, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0010nx0kmfo348lv', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that. How did you handle real-time or micro-batch data processing in those microservices?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 9, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0011nx0kiv53y2qd', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Just a quick check—could you give me an example of how you handled real-time data in one of those Kafka-based microservices?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 10, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0012nx0kux030jl8', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'Ok, so I designed an event-based architecture where microservices acted both as a producer and a consumer, leveraging Kafka to handle high-throughput stream for the banking transaction. And I utilized the Kafka Streams API to perform stateful transactions and aggregation on the incoming transaction data, allowing for the real-time validation and fraud detection before committing to the database.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 11, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0013nx0k3jqq22wo', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'For the microbatching for scenarios requiring complex deconsolidation, I implemented Spring Batch integrated with Kafka, which processed incoming records in micro batches to balance latency and system resource utilization. Also, I configured Kafka partition strategies and consumer groups to ensure horizontal scalability and maintain strict ordering of events, which was critical for the financial data integrity. To ensure zero data loss during the processing, I enabled acknowledgement-based messaging and implemented idempotent consumer patterns, ensuring that even if the event of the port failure or network hiccup, the system state remained consistent.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 12, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0014nx0kal3h2cyw', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that. Now, how about your experience with graph technologies like Neo4j and handling graph data modeling?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 13, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0015nx0k9ny8vyj9', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I have experience in working on both graph data structure to map complex relationships, particularly when dealing with interconnected data points in financial applications where traditional relation models becomes inefficient. I have utilized graph-based approaches to identify patterns such as fraud detection or dependency mapping by traversing nodes and relationships rather than relying on multiple execution of operation in SQL databases.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 14, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0016nx0kofku9lz1', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'In my architecture work, I have integrated graph data tools with microservices to handle high-link datasets, ensuring that the schema design supports both efficient retrieval and scalability. While my primary expertise lies in SQL, Postgres, and NoSQL database systems, I stay updated with emerging technologies and am comfortable applying graph theory to optimize data-heavy workflows that requires deeply analysis.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 15, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0017nx0kz3axai9g', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now, can you share your experience working with LLM-integrated systems or AI-driven architectures?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 16, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0018nx0kxvt8sncq', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'I have actively leveraged GitHub Copilot in my recent role in PNC to accelerate the development lifecycle, improving the code quality and expertise in the and expedite the debugging process, which has significantly reduced our time to migrate to market for the microservices. My experience includes integrating AI-driven tools into CI/CD pipeline to automate routine tasks, thereby allowing the teams to focus only on the backend logic and architecture improvements. While my core background is high scalable Java backend system, I have been exploring and implementing prompt-based engineering to optimize the SQL query generation and performance complex refactoring ensuring that the code meets our performance and compliance standards. I''m focused on architecting backend services that are AI-ready, ensuring that our data models where in Oracle, PostgreSQL, or NoSQL stores are structured to easily feed into LLM pipelines for future predictive analytics and automated reporting features. I stay updated with the latest AI framework to ensure that our technical vision remains competitive, specifically evaluating how LLM can be integrated to troubleshoot legacy codebase during migration projects.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 17, null), ('cmp6y6v6f0019nx0kgmfhgid2', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Appreciate that detail. One last question: how do you approach integrating CI/CD pipelines in enterprise environments?', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 18, null), ('cmp6y6v6f001anx0k515ry197', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I''m focused on implementing build once, deploy many principle utilizing Jenkins and Maven to ensure consistency across the environment. I''ll leverage Terraform and Docker to define environmental configuration, ensuring the infrastructure is version controlled, repeatable, and scalable across AWS and Azure. And I integrated automated unit testing, which is like JUnit and Mockito, and quality gates such as SonarQube directly into the CI/CD pipeline to ensure that only code meeting performance and security standards progresses to production. I favor blue-green pattern deployment strategies with Kubernetes to minimize the downtime and mitigation risk during the releases. I work closely with DevOps teams to streamline the transition from development to operation, ensuring that monitoring and logging are integrated into the pipeline to allow for rapid troubleshooting post-deployment.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 19, null), ('cmp6y6v6f001bnx0k3lu776gz', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'In enterprise environment, I emphasize embedding security scanning in the pipeline to maintain audit releases and adherence to strict regulatory requirements.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 20, null), ('cmp6y6v6f001cnx0ksioktn7c', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you, Deepak. That covers the key areas. I appreciate your time today. We''ll be in touch soon. Take care.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 21, null), ('cmp6y6v6f001dnx0ko7ry2lk5', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'CANDIDATE', 'Thank you. Good day.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 22, null), ('cmp6y6v6f001enx0kwwxksc34', 'cmp6xv92v000pnx0k28756ltz', 'INTERVIEWER', 'You too, Deepak. Have a great day ahead.', '2026-05-15 13:23:12.855', 23, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001snx0kynu9zd8q', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'então', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 0, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001tnx0k33y7st2r', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Naveen, this is your interview for the Senior Data Engineer and AI/ML Engineer role. Let’s get started. Can you briefly introduce your current role and the kind of projects you''re working on right now?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 1, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001unx0kqg3djazh', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, you know, let''s talk about some of the projects. So in my current client, you know, that is a Home Depot, I''ve been focusing on the agent data pipelines that handles a lot of operational stuff, you know, without any constant human intervention. The big project is like I''ve been creating the intelligence system that mounts our third-party vendor feeds. Basically, we get like product catalog updates, pricing changes, and inventory levels from hundreds of suppliers. And you know, the quality is everywhere. So I''m going to use like LangChain and LangGraph. It''s kind of to build the agents that can detect any anomalies, figuring out, you know, what''s going on wrong. In some cases, I need to be fixing the issues as well, based on the root, to an example right there. So and also, you know, the other piece is to handle the real-time pipelines in the Apache airflow, because that moves our data mainly into our snowflake warehouse, mainly into operational systems. And we are going to, you know, pushing the aggregate inventory as well into our Salesforce from the sales operational team. So there will be a rise of the stock levels when the teams is going to be working with different, different clients. And you know, this involves the Mulesoft integrations as well with the different clients that involves a lot of, you know, Mulesoft integrations, I would say, to customer.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 2, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001vnx0kvl81kukc', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for sharing that. Let''s dive deeper into your experience. What agentic AI workflow have you built in production, and how did it operate end-to-end?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 3, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001wnx0kgv4suo0c', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, you know, when we talk about this context, mainly let''s talk about the data quality challenges first, because, you know, we are dealing with a lot of vendor feeds and the building intelligence as well into our pipeline. So when I am building these agents, this will detect, you know, the anomalies and fix the issues. So I''ve been, you know, approaching the different things like confident thresholds, because that''s gonna decide what''s get routed, you know, to a human where it''s fixed. So on the real-time pipeline, I''ll be going with the airflow that''s gonna, you know, pushing our Salesforce into the difference framing, and it''s a more kind of a microbatch setup. So, you know, I''m very curious to set up an airflow. That''s kind of batch oriented. So I was wondering, you know, to use if any airflow sensors. That''s gonna trigger, you know, automatically. And I''ll be going with the MuleSoft integrations as well. This kind of, you know, transformation logic mainly built within the MuleSoft itself, or I will be going with the heavy lifting in Python, you know, tons of MuleSoft here.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 4, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001xnx0kcyvzup7u', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How did you integrate LLM APIs into your existing data pipelines?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 5, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001ynx0kf8ohpmhg', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. What real-world problem did you solve using LangChain or CrewAI?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 6, null), ('cmp6zrp2v001znx0kveo0vls6', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, you know, when we talk about the LLM APIs, first I will be going with LLM API integration. This kind of, you know, do the specific checkpoints across the pipeline where we need the reason capabilities. So initially I''ll be going with the data validation layer. That''s going to run the standard schema checks, null checks, and data type validation as well. If anything fails, right, or the group suspicious, I''ll be calling, you know, to intelligent layer. And I''ll be going to build in Python module that''s wrap up the open API calls. And that is the context as well. So when I record the validation, right, the module simply puts the file records together. And, you know, expert in the schema to our data dictionary within our Snowflake warehouse. And the examples are from our vector source, you know, the key thing I''ll be going with the functional calling within a open AI because, you know, that will be giving the structured JSON to the pipeline so that can actually work with. And there will be, you know, different issues as well before between the zero and one confidence score. So it''s about the 0.85 the pipeline automatically fix the if there is any bugs in like that. And it will be creating the tickets as well within our monitoring system. And for the airflow integration, I''ll be creating the customer engines as well so that we''ll be having the DAG, right, that''s gonna run for every hour for the incoming files. And we''ll be having a lot of records as well, you know, 800 to 1200 per hour. Everything is getting close, yeah.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 7, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0020nx0k6ptm129c', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, you know, when we talk about this LangChain and CoE, we''ll be dealing with a lot of problems. In my current one, let me explain to you some scenario. We''ll be handling, you know, massive pain point of the supply data onboarding, so that we''ll be getting new suppliers, right? They''ll be having the catalogs in different formats, might be from CSV or Excel, sometimes maybe from the PDFs as well. So everything is, you know, getting the field mapping, it never be consistent. So the supplier, you know, will be having the item number, and you can call this as SKU. So there will be like product ID, you know, that''s all this way to be a supplier just from doing like manual mapping before validation. And I''ll be laying a blank graph agent as well, that item is most of that, like having the multiple stages because it frustrates the incoming file, you know, hiding thing, the structure, and it will convert to a canonical data model. So third agent will be the snowflake, you know, it will follow some of the mapping rules as well. The pretty cool part is, you know, with the LangGras trade machine, because each supplier will be getting inserted from the different parts in the workflow. So look like, you know, file has embedded readers or multiple sheets, right? It will be going to the extraction step first. Then, you know, I''d be using GPT-4 version as well, mainly for the mapping agents, because that''s kind of a contest. I will be looking, you know, with a sample with an end product description. Then I''ll be building a RAG pipeline as well, that''s one of filling up the supplier pipelines. We are done well before with the PineCore, but so that, you know, the agent can check the historical patterns, I would say.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 8, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0021nx0kwpo296dh', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks, that’s helpful. How did you optimize RAG pipeline accuracy or response quality?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 9, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0022nx0kp7u1vzf4', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'Can you repeat the question?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 10, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0023nx0k3r55gzzd', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Certainly. How did you optimize RAG pipeline accuracy or response quality?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 11, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0024nx0kddvbk6if', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, you know, when we talk about this raw pipeline accuracy, the biggest issue I would say is the retrieval step that was pulling up mainly relevant checks, especially into our supplied information, so that it was kind of domain specific. Initially, it was doing a cosine symmetry, kind of a you know, hambering stuff, and it would make a lot of noise. So I''ll be going with the implement hybrid approach, you''re right, to the different keyword search, maybe like BM25. I''ll be running, you know, in a board parallel and doing a weighted match, completed the results. For the use case, I''ll be going with a weighting of the 80% semantic and 30% of will be going with your keyboard stuff, because I''ll be having, you know, pure semantic search misses. And there will be a chunking strategies as well. That''s made a very huge difference. I''ll be going to fix, you know, five, four token chunks within the same, like some might be overlapping, right? Some might be spreading based on the information. So I''ll be simply switching to a semantic chunking where I''ll be using a sentence boundaries, keeping related, you know, paragraphs together and it will be existing as well, keeping the main context. And finally, I can add the metadata filtering as well before the similar event runs so that, you know, each chunk gets be tagged to a particular, you know, metadata, supply type or might be a document date. So I will be going with the re-ranking step as well. That''s kind of critical stuff where we''ll be having different 20 candidates running with the cross-ended model. So I can use like, you know, mini LM ranker that''s going to actually understand the query document. Yeah.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 12, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0025nx0ks9rtlto2', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. Next, what complex ETL workflow did you build using Python and Airflow?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 13, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0026nx0k9ejd5r1e', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, you know, coming to the complex ETL pipeline, I would say is like my current life, let me give you one more scenario. We''ll be having the ETL workflow that will be consolidating the pricing data, mainly from the multiple region systems into our Snowflake. The challenge was these regional systems, you know, update at different times throughout the day. So they need to maintain the price change history while also, you know, need to be focusing on real-time updates to our e-commerce platform. And I''ll be building, you know, Airflow as well within a custom Python operators because of kind of out of the box stuffing. It''s not, you know, cutting earlier. So I''ll be running the DAG every two hours by branching up the logic based on the freshness checks, you know, so that we''ll be getting six different source systems in terms of the watermark timestamps. If you know which region has some new data, right, it will trigger that branch. It won''t skip generally. So other thing would be the Python modules. I would handle the incremental logic, right, with the different bricks, maybe in kind of, you know, promotional pricing separately. I can build a factory pattern as well, so that we''ll be getting each source, mainly from the base class, identifying, you know, source to specific transformations. And the tricky part, I would say, is the price conflicts because we''ll be having the SKU. It''s kind of different prices updating within the regions within the same run. So I can do a reconciliation module as well. That''s gonna bring the business rules like the cooperative pricing. And mainly finding the orchestration side, I''ll be going with, you know, task flow API. It''s kind of dynamic task masking. We do have the SLA set up on a critical part with no longer than 90 minutes, I would say.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 14, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0027nx0kjx224v2v', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I see. How did you troubleshoot failures in real-time data pipelines?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 15, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0028nx0kcgndss68', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, you know, when we talk about the troubleshooting of the stuff, we''ll be going with the monitoring dashboards. We do set up a data log in my current slide, you know, we are streaming a supplier updates to our Kafka. That''s going on a matrix on the consumer leg. I''ll be going with the message to put it as well, where we''ll be having different error rates, like the lag spiking, so that, you know, the consumers will be getting the model next stream. We''ve been jumping with the airflow logs or the application logs, depending where the failure is exactly. So I''ll be going with the real-time pipelines, dealing with, you know, data quality issues, like malformed JSON or the schema mismatches. So one common thing is I''ve seen, you know, this message type causes the consumer to crash generally. So I''ll be wrapping up the logs through a particular traces. And I''ll be going with the dead letter queue as well to see what the exact message is going to fail. And I''ll be going with the schema issue. If that is the case, I''ll be going with the Avro schemas. It''s kind of, you know, schema registry that will be going with the proper versioning. So if anything happens, right, it will simply consume the code to handle both schemas temporarily. On the performance degradation, I''ll be looking up the processing time per message. And I''ll also check if there is any database connection within our, you know, API calls to downstream the systems and on the Salesforce API rate, you know, the limits one going to be back off as well. Final thing is about the recon string. It''s kind of resource stuff. We''ll be getting different consumer instances here, like messaging volume, and it''s kind of big supplier refresh, so that the consumers can''t keep everything. So I''ll be going with the consumer group to manage model processing. Yeah.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 16, null), ('cmp6zrp2v0029nx0kk8cspmrq', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. What multi-step automation project did you own end-to-end?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 17, null), ('cmp6zrp2v002anx0k1cqrpzi0', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'So in kind of, you know, multi-step project, I''ll be going with my previous client here. So I want end-to-end automation, mainly for the merchant onboarding reconciliation. The process was, you know, we''ll be having the analyst, where we''re getting the merchant''s data from the partner banks. We''ll be validating, you know, against the compliance rules with the cross-reference teams and the merchant databases. And I''ll be going with three to four days per batch of a merchant. And here I decided with five shop agenting workflow, mainly using Langchain and GPT-4, because it''s firstly extract the merchant details from various formats, might be kind of CSV or PDFs, sometimes might be scanned documents using those here. It''s normalize everything, right, within the standard schema, so that, you know, it will be going with the compliance validation by checking against the validation tag side is verifying the registration numbers. And the third agent is kind of interesting, I would say, like a free image matching, existing within our existing database, within our Snowflake, because to avoid any potential duplicates here. And using with the vector embedding stores, I''ll be going with a pine code, mainly for the semantic similarity. And I''ll be going with, you know, McDonald''s Corporation as well. They will be coming in. If there are any flags, right, the agent score simply matches that and create some kind of confidence rating. And the final thing is kind of risk assessment based on the category codes, transaction history, maybe from the geography risk factors as well. These are the routing and notifications, close.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 18, null), ('cmp6zrp2v002bnx0k2mslaes6', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for explaining that. We’ve covered the main areas. Just one last question: what motivates you most about working on agentic AI-driven data engineering solutions?', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 19, null), ('cmp6zrp2v002cnx0kiz4ngmbp', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'CANDIDATE', 'So coming to this question, I would say like I do accept a lot of things, right, mainly in terms of solving problems that removes the friction for the people because I''ve been spending a year with traditional ETL pipelines because they are completely reliable. They are rigid as well. So we need to be every rule here in terms of hard coding. I''ve been going with every edge case as well because the moment requirements, you know, charge your back in the code. So with the agenting systems, there is a lot of new dimensions in terms of adaptability because in my current line we are doing with the data ingestion systems so that the agents clearly handle the certain variations within a different formats without me as well, like, you know, writing a millions of statements. If a supplier, you know, sends the data within a different structure, the agent simply figured itself out what exactly needed and what it''s kept moving. Yeah, and you know, these are all things like motivate me in terms of the operational impact as well.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 20, null), ('cmp6zrp2v002dnx0km8bnks8p', 'cmp6z6r0f001knx0kbdqeza9g', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Great to hear that. Thank you, Naveen. That wraps up our interview. We appreciate your time and insights. We''ll be in touch soon. Take care.', '2026-05-15 14:07:24.343', 21, null), ('cmp70ad0j002unx0ko6tjcuc1', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello, can you hear me?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 0, null), ('cmp70ad0j002vnx0k2wml9h86', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Yes, I can hear you clearly. Let’s get started. Please introduce yourself and tell me a bit about your current role.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 1, null), ('cmp70ad0j002wnx0kf200gh17', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure. Okay, so I have experience as a Scrum Master, more or less 10 years of experience, and my career role is a mixed combination between Scrum Master and Project Manager. My responsibilities as a Scrum Master are to help the team in the agile framework, with some scalable activities or actions. And my responsibilities as a Project Manager is to track the project as a high level, ensure that the milestones are achieved, and be sure that we have everything in place for the deliverable that we need to complete.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 2, null), ('cmp70ad0j002xnx0kntxdpfuy', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that. Let’s dive into some specifics. How many Agile teams have you managed simultaneously?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 3, null), ('cmp70ad0j002ynx0kj7w3q3g7', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'In the past I have been working with four different teams simultaneously.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 4, null), ('cmp70ad0j002znx0kxoaqdq2e', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. And can you tell me about an Agile transformation initiative that you led recently?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 5, null), ('cmp70ad0j0030nx0kuo3742yg', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, well, I was part of one transition between waterfall into the agile framework. In this case, we defined a mixed agile framework, so a scrum with some ceremonies as a scalable framework. So we have the daily standup, planning, retrospective, sprint demo, backlog refinement. Plus we add a planning for the next three months, pretty similar to a PI planning.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 6, null), ('cmp70ad0j0031nx0kg1re3c21', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'And also a PIJ.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 7, null), ('cmp70ad0j0032nx0k2bzhh6ar', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you handle repeated sprint spillovers or missed commitments during that transformation?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 8, null), ('cmp70ad0j0033nx0kjm01sprc', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Well, in that case, it was a little hard because we have a lot of spillovers, sprint by sprint, that happens until the team gets the maturity to understand and move together into the transformation. But at the beginning, we need to plan a little bit lower than we used to have. And also, we need to escalate a lot of topics with the different layers that we have. But when the team gets familiar, then we start using better estimations and we reduce the spillovers.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 9, null), ('cmp70ad0j0034nx0kgl8gbh2v', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for explaining that. What Jira or ADO dashboards did you create for leadership tracking?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 10, null), ('cmp70ad0j0035nx0k12m9iman', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'In both cases, I have worked with different dashboards with different metrics, but the main metrics are the velocity, predictability, and all the items that are completed versus the planning at the beginning of the sprint.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 11, null), ('cmp70ad0j0036nx0ki3h5c15r', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you resolve conflicts between engineering and business teams during these projects?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 12, null), ('cmp70ad0j0037nx0k5x5abrvz', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'If we are going, if we can go into more detail, we can, I have created dashboards for tracking specific activities for each developer or tester, and or a user story that we have for every iteration and the status for them.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 13, null), ('cmp70ad0j0038nx0kkk2lyl69', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Well, first of all, I need to set up the communication channels with the business and the tech leads or QA leads to discuss the root cause analysis, understand the input from the business, and go into a midpoint where we can be aligned from both parts.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 14, null), ('cmp70ad0j0039nx0kx5vyzg62', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. What’s one impediment you removed that significantly improved delivery speed?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 15, null), ('cmp70ad0j003anx0kyjber3x5', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'One of them is communication between the developers and the testers.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 16, null), ('cmp70ad0j003bnx0kwexfphn4', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'we are not able, the team was not able to complete 80% of the work that was planned at the beginning of the iteration, and that was because all the developers hand over their work when they are completely done. So this is not what we are expecting, because with that, the testers don''t have enough time to complete the work. So what we place is a handover immediately as every developer completes any task, they hand over to QA so they can share or hand over the work to QA in an incremental way, so that can give enough time for the testers to complete the work.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 17, null), ('cmp70ad0j003cnx0k9cfvrkuy', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Makes sense. How have you handled dependencies across multiple Scrum teams?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 18, null), ('cmp70ad0j003dnx0kizb10y7h', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Well, we have different channels of communication, but one of them is that we need to start the escalations, we need to share the inputs with other Scrum masters, we need to schedule the calls, and also we need to keep the RT in touch and updated on every step that we are doing related to the impediments.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 19, null), ('cmp70ad0j003enx0k66pwfjbk', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Have you worked as a Lead before? What was the team size?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 20, null), ('cmp70ad0j003fnx0kazwkt4a4', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, I have been working as a lead in the past, and my team was of 15 members split in four teams.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 21, null), ('cmp70ad0j003gnx0kinmd3h4s', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. One final question: how did you handle situations with multiple missed commitments across those teams?', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 22, null), ('cmp70ad0j003hnx0kbydymieq', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay, well, I need to track them in a specific way, so I create minutes, I create action items, and I track all of them during my day.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 23, null), ('cmp70ad0j003inx0ko300w6af', 'cmp701p00002lnx0km27w4j2e', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Thank you for walking through your approach. That concludes our interview. We appreciate your time and insights. Take care.', '2026-05-15 14:21:55.171', 24, null), ('cmp71dqnj004lnx0krdh7jfig', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 0, null), ('cmp71dqnj004mnx0kvx0taz8t', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Rohit, thank you for joining. I’m going to be conducting your interview for the Senior Data Engineer role today. Let’s get started. Could you give me a brief overview of your background and current role?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 1, null), ('cmp71dqnk004nnx0katfhly2w', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure. Hi, I''m a data engineer with around two years of experience of IT experience, mainly focused on cloud-based data engineer and ETL and ELT pipelines development and enterprise analytics performance platforms. In my recent projects, I''ve worked extensively with Azure Databricks, PySpark, SQL, and Snowflake, and Azure Data Factory, and ADLS, and Genetic2 build scalable data pipelines and modern data lake architecture. At the state of Ohio, I supported models like organization registrations, payment processing, and annual report filing, where I designed and maintained the production-grade pipelines processing large enterprise datasets. I also worked on migrating legacy SAS workflows into the database with clients and improving processing efficiency, reducing the batch runtimes, and minimizing the manual operational effect. Along with the development, I handled the monitoring, troubleshooting, and root cause analysis, and performance optimizations for enterprise-scale data platforms.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 2, null), ('cmp71dqnk004onx0ke35brmal', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that summary. Let’s dive in. Can you tell me about a complex ETL workflow you built using Python and Airflow?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 3, null), ('cmp71dqnk004pnx0k55opqczq', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, I have a strong hands-on experience designing and developing ETL pipelines using Databricks, PySpark, Python, and Snowflake. My work involved ingesting data from relational databases, APIs, and cloud storage and enterprise systems into the ADLS and cloud-based lakehouse platforms. I performed transformations, including cleaning, joins, aggregates, validations, and business rules implementing the PySpark and Spark SQL before loading created data set into the Snowflake and the reporting systems. I also implement scheduling, monitoring, and retime mechanisms and logging to improve stability and operational stability.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 4, null), ('cmp71dqnk004qnx0knzvmnd6r', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you troubleshoot a failing production data pipeline in that context?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 5, null), ('cmp71dqnk004rnx0k9b3debpa', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'So one of the major issues I would say in my recent project, we had recurring failing in high volume nightly ETL jobs caused by script joins and insufficient parsing. I analyzed Spark execution logs, identifying the bottlenecks, and redesigned the transformation logic and optimized joins and tuned the cluster configuration. As a result, the ETL runtime was reduced significantly, and pipeline stability improved and manual operational intervention was minimized.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 6, null), ('cmp71dqnk004snx0k1ooicihr', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Now, what Snowflake query optimization did you implement that improved performance significantly?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 7, null), ('cmp71dqnk004tnx0kavhhn6u1', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'I worked with Snowflake as a cloud data warehouse, supporting the enterprise analytics and reporting workloads. I worked with including loading curated data sets from the Databricks into Snowflake, writing optimized SQL queries, and creating reporting data sets, and supporting Power BI dashboards for analytics users. I also worked with structured and semi-structured data formats such as JSON and Paracet and supporting data validation and optimization and performance tuning activities.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 8, null), ('cmp71dqnk004unx0k7nk7919c', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Could you share one specific Snowflake query optimization that really boosted performance?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 9, null), ('cmp71dqnk004vnx0k3i8ppl64', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'In one scenario, I would say, uh, like, it''s a cloud database platform, like, uh, designed mainly. One of the key advantage of Snowflake is like uh separation of compute and storage where uh data set can be uh used and uh independent, scalable, and performance, uh better performance optimization. In my experience, I worked with Snowflakes for uh storing uh curated data sets uh with coming from the ETL pipelines and uh performance uh SQL-based transformations and uh supporting the uh downstream power BI uh reporting and uh analytic usage.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 10, null), ('cmp71dqnk004wnx0kvr6cfe4l', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I see. Could you pinpoint a single query change or technique that improved performance significantly?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 11, null), ('cmp71dqnk004xnx0k7pzsb1nn', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'So in my recent project with the state of Ohio, like the data was integrated from multiple operational systems such as organizations and registrations and payment processing and annual report filing applications into the data lake through Databricks and ADF pipelines. Using the PySpark and Spark SQL, we transformed and validated the data sets before loading the data into the Snowflake tables, and business and compliance teams then used the Power BI dashboards connected to the Snowflakes to track registrations and payment collections or like filing compliance. And I was involved in designing SQL transformations, like optimizing queries, handle the semi-Structured data formats like JSON, and improving the performance for the large analytic workloads.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 12, null), ('cmp71dqnk004ynx0kf3t1ar3z', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let’s move on. How have you handled real-time data ingestion in production?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 13, null), ('cmp71dqnk004znx0kl17pry50', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'So one typical scenario I would say when we are dealing with the production, like in one of the scenarios I was working with the AEP American Electric Power, where we had a workload data continuously generating from multiple enterprise systems such as AWS RDS, Aurora, and SQL Server. We used Databricks and Kafka-based streaming pipelines to ingest near real-time events into the data lake platforms. After injections like PySpark tasks were valid and standard the incoming records before loading the curated datasets into the snowflake, where snowflake acted as a centralized analytics warehouse where business teams accessed operational dashboards through Power BI and for the outage management and workforce analytics and capacity planning. One important production challenge I was handling increasing data volumes like query latency during peak operational hours. To improve that performance, we optimized the SQL workload using the cluster strategies, tuning the query, and incrementing the loading patterns and transforming from the Databricks. So this helped improve the dashboard response times and supported more than 200 analytical users and reduced overall ETL runtime significantly while maintaining the stable production SLS.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 14, null), ('cmp71dqnk0050nx0kxzq6t944', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. What Salesforce data integrations have you worked on directly?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 15, null), ('cmp71dqnk0051nx0kcuh11me5', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'So typically on Salesforce, I would say like in my recent project, we like Salesforce acted as a CRM and customer-related option data, and we extracted data from Salesforce objects such as accounts, cases, and transactional records using the API-based injections, like integrated them into our cloud data platforms. The first data was landed into ADLS through Databricks, and then processed using the PySpark for cleaning and duplications and standardizations. After transformations, reduced datasets were loaded into Snowflake for enterprise reporting and analytics. This data was used by business teams for customer tracking, operational reporting, and performance dashboards in the Power BI. I also worked in handling incremental loads, ensuring the data consistency and monitoring pipelines failure during the Salesforce data injection into the production environment. So I worked on integrating Salesforce data into data platforms using API data, like API-based injections, transforming it using the Databricks and PySpark, and loading it into the Snowflake for reporting and analytics use cases.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 16, null), ('cmp71dqnk0052nx0kgqghjppn', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you implement data quality checks in your pipelines?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 17, null), ('cmp71dqnk0053nx0k8kvm0c8a', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I would say like implementing the data quality checks in my recent project, data quality was a crucial part of the pipeline design since we worked with a large scale enterprise and operational data coming from multiple sources like databases, APIs, and stream feeds. To ensure data quality, I implemented multiple validation layers at different states of pipeline. These include the schema validation and null and duplicate checks, data type enforcements, and reconciliation between the target and source systems. In Databricks using PySpark, I applied business rules during transformation layers to filter invalid records and standardize the inconsistent data and ensure like integrity before loading data into snowflakes or data stream analytics layer. So we implemented logging, monitoring, and mechanism using the Azure Data Factory and Databricks matrices to detect failures or unknowns early in the pipeline. So by this approach, help improve data reliability and reduce production issues and ensure the accurate reporting for the business dashboards and analytics users.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 18, null), ('cmp71dqnk0054nx0k45s1ocxr', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. What challenges did you face while working with MuleSoft integrations?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 19, null), ('cmp71dqnk0055nx0kq5wk0hry', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'So one challenge, I would say, mainly dealing while working with the large scale and complex data pipelines where we had the data coming from multiple sources like database APIs and legacy ETL jobs. In several cases, we had data inconsistency and schema changes and pipeline failure in the production, especially during the peak batch processing windows. Another challenge was performance issue in Spark jobs with some transformations were slowed due to large data volumes and skewed joints and insufficient partitioning. To handle this, I analyzed Spark execution plans and logs, optimizing the joints using the broadcast techniques, and improve partition strategies and tune the cluster configuration in Databricks. So by implementing proper monitoring, logging, and incremental progressive strategies, we are able to stabilize pipelines and reduce failures in the movesoft and improve overall performance in the production.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 20, null), ('cmp71dqnk0056nx0kvo70u9wv', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that. One last question: what’s the most complex data architecture you’ve designed, and why?', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 21, null), ('cmp71dqnk0057nx0k3vz0831m', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'CANDIDATE', 'I would say one of the key challenges I worked with designing and maintaining scalable data architecture for enterprise-level data platforms, like we''re handling the large volumes of structured or semi-structured data. We had multiple source systems feeding data into platforms. The challenge was to design consistent and scalable architecture that could support the batch and real-time processing. Another challenge was ensuring proper data flow across multiple layers, like for injections, processing, and service layer, while maintaining data quality and performance. I addressed this by implementing the mediation architecture in Databricks, like bronze, silver, and gold layers using the ADLS and data lakes, which helped standardize data processing and improve maintainability. By this, we also optimized the architecture of performance using the partition strategy and incremental loads and efficient spark transformations, which improved processing time and system reliability. The main challenge was designing scalable data architecture for large data sets across multiple systems. So I solved it using the mediation architecture in Databricks with ADLS and data lakes, ensuring that scalability and performance and data consistency.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 22, null), ('cmp71dqnk0058nx0kf6r5q0zz', 'cmp70s8to004dnx0kr6xvyaz5', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that. We’ve covered the key areas. That’s all for today’s interview. We’ll be in touch soon. Take care.', '2026-05-15 14:52:32.432', 23, null), ('cmp72tayb005onx0kix03zw4w', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 0, null), ('cmp72tayb005pnx0kpoz8s7no', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Srinivas, good to meet you. I''m going to be your interviewer today. Let''s dive right in. Could you start', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 1, null), ('cmp72tayb005qnx0kac5q5c7s', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hey, how are you?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 2, null), ('cmp72tayb005rnx0kwts0r07u', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I''m doing well, thank you. Let''s begin. Can you tell me about your current role and your main responsibilities?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 3, null), ('cmp72tayb005snx0kj46qfqj8', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for sharing that. Let''s dive into some specific projects. What microservices did you build using Java or Node.js recently?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 4, null), ('cmp72tayb005tnx0kj87umj1z', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, I''m currently working as a, like I said, I''m Srinivas Kalyan Yellanki. I''m currently working as a Senior Software Engineer at Expedia. I work into a team called Incentives and Personalization Platform team, which is like a backend as well as a data platform team. So what we do here in the team is we build personalization signals that can be used within the Expedia, within the teams within the Expedia where they can, you know, you know, like look at the, so basically we provide the users personalized signals which can be used by these teams within the Expedia so that, you know, they can use this information for showing better travel traveler recommendations. So we expose this data from our team through GRPC API as well as the SDK. And the tech stack that we use is Java, Kotlin for development of this GRPC API as well as the SDK. We use Kafka as a streaming platform and the we use Apache Spark for data batch processing. And I think, yeah, pretty much that''s like a tech stack. Cassandra is a data store, by the way. And prior to this, I worked at various other companies, but this is my current work at Expedia.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 5, null), ('cmp72tayb005unx0kmtbfl97k', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Recently, Java, no microservices, I built, you know, using Java like REST endpoints.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 6, null), ('cmp72tayb005vnx0krdeunj05', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How did you design those APIs for high-traffic distributed systems?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 7, null), ('cmp72tayb005wnx0k7swcumpd', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Well, you know, I make sure each and every Every functionality or operational aspect of the microservices is broken down into different endpoints where, you know, like, you know, like each functionality is doing its own specific job and it''s exposed to an endpoint. For example, and you know, like, for example, you know, like a GET only performs get operations, you know, from the database, and, you know, post operations will do any sort of changes to the database, you know, writing a new record to the database. And of course, you know, like, we do use put, delete, and patch as well, just in case if we want to change or delete the records from the database. And I also make sure, you know, for attaining the distributed nature, I''ll make sure the APIs are in stateless nature. Uh yeah.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 8, null), ('cmp72tayb005xnx0kojr7ddj3', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Can you share a real production issue you debugged in a microservices environment?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 9, null), ('cmp72tayb005ynx0kwjsl6dq5', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'That’s a thorough debugging process. How have you used Neo4j in real-world projects?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 10, null), ('cmp72tayb005znx0koqaduhsm', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Microsoft vs environment. So there was this recent issue that I came across where the P99 was like, you know, for one of the endpoint that we exposed was breaching our SLAs, you know, like maybe, you know, our SLA was like, you know, 980 milliseconds, but that was taking like close to 300 milliseconds. So, uh, and this was like, you know, it was very highly sensitive API. So, uh, I mean, like I said, you know, it was the latency was so high that, you know, which was breaking our SLAs. So the way how I debugged was, you know, like looked into Splunk logs to see, you know, like how much set of traffic was really impacted with this high latency and isolated that, you know, it''s not causing for all the customers or whether it is, whether it is impacting only a group of customers or, you know, like the entire service, you know, like for the entire all all the user base. So I identified, you know, like where exactly, you know, what exactly the impact was and who exactly are the impacted customers and drilled down to see what exactly happened here. I went to see the root cause analysis. What I did was, uh, so, so what happened was like, you know, uh uh the latency was so high because, you know, like the uh Cassandra was, you know, like one of the data store that we were using, you know, like for this particular for this particular input. But there is also another data store that we use uh to provide this data, which is a downstream service. Okay, a downstream service. Uh, so what happened was like, you know, this downstream service was the issue where, you know, it was, uh it was taking uh more time than what we assumed. So I identified the issue was coming from the downstream service and engaged the downstream service to see uh worked closely with them to see, you know, like what has changed, uh, you know, like from, you know, basically identified from what time the issue has started and uh narrowed it down to, you know, like uh what time, what like what was the group of users that got impacted with that with that information, you know, like I went ahead and, you know, like talked to the downstream team as an immediate mitigation plan, you know, like we, we identified what was the change, new change that was introduced from the downstream service and you know, like enabled the, you know, like uh uh on my product side, you know, I enabled graceful degradation so that, you know, like any further requests are not, you know, like uh uh impacted uh with this high latency. So immediately worked with the downstream service to, you know, like ask them to reload uh uh roll back to the previous change. So did two things, you know, like enabled graceful degradation as well as requested the downstream service to roll back to the previous version until, you know, we figure out what was the issue. With this, I was able to attend the, you know, like stability in the P99 latency, you know, the downtime latency of P99 was taken care.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 11, null), ('cmp72tayb0060nx0kzmz0lxhm', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'So Neo4j is like one of the graphical database that I have used, you know, like in my one of the, in one of my project within the Expedia. So, you know, instead of having all relational or document level of, you know, like tables or, you know, like a data store, I wanted to, you know, like, we used, you know, like a Neo4j, Neo4j, you know, like database where, you know, like each and every, every, every, you know, like a data is like stored into like in the form of nodes.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 12, null), ('cmp72tayb0061nx0ke7b4j265', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'And also, you know, like establish the relationship with that.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 13, null), ('cmp72tayb0062nx0kcd7jqotv', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Can you describe a Knowledge Graph implementation you directly contributed to?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 14, null), ('cmp72tayb0063nx0ktmsuqx7k', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Knowledge graph. So, I mean, like, you know, I can take an example there, but I think knowledge graph is, you know, like one of the, so I know like it has entities, you know, the entities are like, you know, the relationships in a graph structure, right? So I can give an example, you know, like the use case that I was talking about. I have this Chrome extension, you know, like where, where we showcase or where we show the users a particular user, you know, like all the context information, you know, like, as I said, you know, like my team was like incentives and personalization team for a user, for a user, you know, like they can, they can, you know, like see what all personalized information for a given, for a given user is, you know, like stored into our system. So I primarily use for this Chrome extension, you know, like these graphical representation, implementation for ranking purposes, you know, like for better ranking, for better recommendations ranking.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 15, null), ('cmp72tayb0064nx0kjmkl3xlh', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that example. How did you integrate LLMs with graph or semantic systems in your work?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 16, null), ('cmp72tayb0065nx0krpn07u3h', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'I think I did like in multiple, multiple, multiple, you know, integrations I''ve done. One example was, you know, for the reporting. So basically, the data that we deal with right now is all about, you know, like a customer, you know, like what exactly their historical information was. And, you know, for a customer, let''s take an example, customer A, they can have, you know, like origin airport context, meaning, you know, like what exactly their origin airport is. What exactly that user''s origin airport is. And second one was like, you know, you know, if you look at the user''s trip intent or trip context, meaning, you know, like what, whether this user has any trip that is currently in progress, whether the trip is in, you know, like shopping, the user is in shopping phase, or the post-booking, you know, like basically different phases of travel. And the other context could be loyalty context, you know, like whether this particular context, this particular user on Expedia, whether they are a blue member or silver member or gold member. So that gives us the loyalty information of this particular user. So I built some reports where any leadership or anyone can come and, you know, like query the tables to see, you know, like what exactly the overall, you know, like responses from our system was, whether we were responding back with 200, successful, or no data, or, you know, like an error. So this is all, you know, represented in the form of table. Now, with the LLM integration, what I did was, you know, like instead of, you know, talking to the, instead of generating these reports by doing the SQL queries, I made that, you know, happen or possible using this LLM agents where now any user can come and, you know, like to talk to these tables in the natural language. So that, you know, like it''s all, like I built a chat interface, you know, like where any user can come in and, you know, like talk to the, talk to the system with the natural language and get the same, same, you know, like same output.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 17, null), ('cmp72tayb0066nx0k62j9c8kv', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'And also, I use some MCP server to integrate with this QueryBook system, where, you know, this LLM will help me structure the data and also helps me represent this data in various different forms. Of course, you know, like if I''m going with the query-based, it''s only in table-based. Whereas if I do it with the, if I do it in the graph, I think this returns in the form of matching hotels and matching relevant, you know, like relevant flights.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 18, null), ('cmp72tayb0067nx0k5h203jry', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Avarus', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 19, null), ('cmp72tayb0068nx0kks9b7bg8', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Appreciate that detail. Final question: what deployment or CI/CD challenge did you solve recently?', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 20, null), ('cmp72tayb0069nx0kez0lpgvg', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Ah, see, I think I''ll take one example. So basically, you know, like the recent issue that I came across was, you know, like rolling out a particular feature, you know, like from our microservice that we have built. So I made sure, you know, like I had released this, you know, like microservice in terms, you know, like a percentage basis, you know, like something like a kernel deployments where, you know, like increase the traffic like, you know, 5%, 10%, 15%. So there, you know, like I ran into an issue where, you know, like the TNLs, which is nothing but test and learn, or nothing but, excuse me, or like in an A-B testing before, you know, pushing that code to prod. It was all working fine for a group of users that we were testing, but once we started rolling out the change to prod, like, you know, started deploying like, you know, 5%, 10%, you know, like incrementing it like in a basically rolling it out in incremental fashion. So there were a few users, you know, like which were not caught because the reason why it was not caught was, you know, like we deal with a lot of users where, you know, like a user that is already locked into Expedia, which is, you know, like where we have a user ID for a logged in user. For a non-logged in user, because anyone can come to Expedia.com and, you know, like without logging into the website, they can also do search for hotels or flights. So we treat them as, you know, like a non-logged in users and we only track their request with the help of device ID. So, you know, like when we were rolling out, you know, like this particular change, you know, like we were bumping from 5 to 10%, you know, like when the traffic came for non-logged in user and even that to particular, you know, like a country, you know, like as we are global, you know, there was this UK users where, you know, when they logged in, UK non-logged in users, when they logged in, when they, you know, started requesting our microservices, you know, like we ran into an issue where I, you know, which we couldn''t catch it in our test and learn or A-B testing before rolling it out to the prod. So, you know, like when we were deploying this to prod, they identified the issue and immediately, you know, rolled it back to a previous version of the service. And then, you know, like went back and, you know, like figured out where exactly the issue was and also identified group of users where this was impacting. And of course, you know, we updated our test suite to include wide variety of users across all the countries, which was, which was something that was lacking before this change was deployed. So that was the root cause analysis.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 21, null), ('cmp72tayb006anx0kb3wa7pbb', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'And then, you know, like it was all monitored on the, while deploying the new rollback, you know, it was all monitored, you know, on the Datadog dashboards and also, you know, like I made sure the alerts were in place so that, you know, like instead of taking a reactive approach, we took the proactive approach by setting, you know, like proper alerts.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 22, null), ('cmp72tayb006bnx0k1tx457i5', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that. I think we''ve covered the key areas. We''ll wrap up here. It was great speaking with you, Srinivas. Thanks for your time, and take care.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 23, null), ('cmp72tayb006cnx0k2fycuz2m', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Thank you.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 24, null), ('cmp72tayb006dnx0kqymod0nb', 'cmp72adee005gnx0kncec3bke', 'CANDIDATE', 'Bye.', '2026-05-15 15:32:38.195', 25, null), ('cmp740lhx0072nx0kdaztkaha', 'cmp73weva006jnx0kwaqagj18', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hi, good morning. This is Navya Krishna Bandaru. I am working as a senior data state data engineer with 10 plus years of experience as ETL and, you know, Snowflake. I have used different kinds of cloud platforms like Azure, AWS, GCP, and I do have experience towards Python, SQL, Snowflake as well. And I am working as, currently I''m working as a senior data engineer, and I have worked, experienced towards multiple domains like mortgage, higher education, healthcare, banking, and insurance and finance as well. I work with data quality, maintaining the data quality, data integration, data maintaining the pipeline management, pipeline monitoring, and as well as the data ingestion. And I do have experience towards Snowflake, SQL, Python, and DB2, Oracle, all these databases. And this role suits my profile because I have seen the profile indicates it is related to the Informatica, which I do have experience in the Snowflake and Python as well. So this is what about me.', '2026-05-15 16:06:18.069', 0, null), ('cmp740lhx0073nx0kh02ipgwa', 'cmp73weva006jnx0kwaqagj18', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Good morning, Navyakrishna. Thanks for that introduction. I appreciate your background, and I understand you''ve worked extensively with ETL, Snowflake, Python, and multiple domains. However, this role is focused on a Software Engineer in Java, particularly with microservices, APIs, and graph technologies like Neo4j. Let''s dive into those areas and see how your experience lines up. To start, could you tell me about a microservice you recently built using Java or Node.', '2026-05-15 16:06:18.069', 1, null), ('cmp740lhx0074nx0kaw6qyg7y', 'cmp73weva006jnx0kwaqagj18', 'CANDIDATE', 'I was told by the interviewer this is related to the snowflake and this is related to all the data engineer positions having experience towards the snowflake and the cloud platforms.', '2026-05-15 16:06:18.069', 2, null), ('cmp740lhx0075nx0kviu8i5nr', 'cmp73weva006jnx0kwaqagj18', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I understand there might have been some confusion earlier. Let me clarify: this particular role is focused on software engineering with Java, microservices, APIs, and graph technologies. Even though your background is strong in data engineering, let''s explore if you’ve had direct experience with Java-based microservices or similar. Can you share any projects where you worked directly with Java microservices or API development?', '2026-05-15 16:06:18.069', 3, null), ('cmp74gvlt007anx0kkl4y7wo0', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Bhargav, thank you for joining the interview today. Let''s get started. I’m going to', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 0, null), ('cmp74gvlt007bnx0kv840m6oe', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Great. So, to kick things off, could you give me a brief introduction about your current role and the kinds of projects you’ve been working on recently?', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 1, null), ('cmp74gvlt007cnx0kp51o1rdk', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that detailed overview. Let’s dive in. What microservices did you build using Java or Node.js recently?', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 2, null), ('cmp74gvlt007dnx0krr1lbrsc', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, so in my recent project, right, so basically I am a full-stack Java developer, so I have experience in complete software development lifecycle from designing, developing, testing, deploying all the complex applications into the cloud platforms as well. So I worked on backend as well as front-end technologies. So when it comes to the backend part, I worked with Java. I have good experience in building microservice architectures. I have strong knowledge in OOPs concepts, core Java concepts, and also I worked on function interfaces, Lambda expressions, stream APIs, and advanced Java features. And also I have used Spring Boot framework, like I worked with Spring MVC, Spring Data JPA, Spring Cloud, Spring Security, where I have implemented both JDBC and OAuth2 for authentication and authorization purpose. And also I have used Spring AMQP as well while working with RabbitMQ and Kafka. In addition to that, I worked on REST APIs and GraphQLs. So along with that, I have very good experience with reactive programming to perform asynchronous operations using Flux and Mono. And on the front-end part, so I worked with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, and also I worked with UI frameworks like React as well as Angular. So I have leveraged all the complex concepts such as I have worked with services, dependency injections, guards, pipes, and all those things. So and also I am proficient using RxJS operators as well. So basically I have worked with structured databases as well as unstructured databases. Like I have used SQL Server, Oracle, MySQL, and also unstructured databases like MongoDB, RedisDB, and also Cosmos DB. I worked especially on GCP platform where I have utilized like I have used and also I worked on AWS as well, like where I have used CloudRun, App Engine, and also I worked on Firestore and all these things. And also I have worked with Terraform as well. So coming to the CI-CD part, so I have used Dockers and Kubernetes to create and manage containers which are used to run the microservices. And also I have used Jenkins for continuous integration and delivery purpose. And also I have used SonarCube and JUnit for code quality and testing purpose. And I have also optimized SQL queries as well. So coming to my previous project, I recently worked with Truest Bank. So here the implementation partner is Cognizant. So here I have worked on migrating a monolithic application to a microservice-based architecture through focusing on the payment service. So here we handled various types of transactions including real-time ACH payments, credit card payments, debit card transactions, as well as wire transfers, P2P transfers, recurring payments, bill payments, and also the mobile wallet transactions as well. So here my primary responsibility was managing all the real-time ACH transactions, like ensuring the secure and efficient processing. So we have developed specialized microservices to handle different aspects of ACH transactions. Like we mainly worked on ACH transaction service. So this is the core service that processes ACH payments including direct deposits, direct debits, P2P transfers, batch processing, and also the recurring payments. So here I have used Spring Security with OAuth2 and JWT to ensure proper authentication and authorization and also to ensure that only authorized users could access the sensitive information. So for the API traffic management, I have utilized Amazon API Gateway, which helped in securing the endpoints as well as load balancing. So when it comes to this payment service, right, so I have used Spring Batch along with executor service. And also I have used completable features to process batch transactions in parallel and in a thread-safe manner. So for recurring payments, I have utilized a cross-scheduler to run the scheduled tasks at regular intervals of time. And to manage the system''s data, I have used a mix of relational databases as well as NoSQL databases. Like we have used PostgreSQL and Oracle and also used MongoDB and RedisDB. And also I have used Apache Kafka for implementing the event-driven messaging systems. So we have enabled asynchronous and reliable message processing to handle the notification services, transaction logs, and also the real-time updates. And also I have implemented Saga design pattern to ensure the transactions failed, earlier steps could be rolled back with the help of compensating transactions. And to optimize the performance, I have applied the CQRS pattern separating the commands from the queries, so allowing for better handling of high-write and high-read operations. So in addition to that, I used Circuit Breaker pattern with Resilience4J. So this is my overall introduction and also what I have been working in my previous project.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 3, null), ('cmp74gvlt007enx0kemv4v1eb', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'So when it comes to that, right, so yeah, I have built a microservices, so in my recent project, and also we have used this for building a real-time ACH transaction service. So here we have specialized a microservices which can handle like different aspects of ACH transaction. So we have our ACH transaction service. So this is one of the core microservices that I would say because it is used to manage the direct deposits, direct debits, P2P transfers, batch processing, and also the recurring payments. It manages the payment completion and it retries the failed transactions and also it handles if there are any issues as well. So the service also connects with the banks and also the financial institutions to process all the payments. So this microservice, right, so we have used different microservice patterns like we have used a circuit breaker pattern, we have used saga design pattern, and also we have used API gateway design pattern. So these are the major patterns that I have used. So when it comes to the Node.js, right, so I have used Node.js as well. So in this project, so.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 4, null), ('cmp74gvlt007fnx0k20c62kqn', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'So when it comes to the Node.js part, right, so in this microservices, so here, so we have basically responsible for developing some of these microservices using Node.js because this Node.js is very good for handling all the asynchronous and also the event-driven workloads as well. So for example, in our ACH processing service, right, so here many operations are IO heavy, which are like input and output heavy operations are to be made, so such as like calling bank APIs, publishing Kafka messages, reading the transaction status as well as sending notifications and also writing the audit logs. So here Node.js, right, so it basically helped us to handle all these operations efficiently using its non-blocking event loop.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 5, null), ('cmp74gvlt007gnx0kfp2dz8em', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'So this is how I have used Node.js in my previous project.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 6, null), ('cmp74gvlt007hnx0kodv9qr4x', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How did you design APIs for high-traffic distributed systems?', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 7, null), ('cmp74gvlt007inx0k3sey8aeq', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'So yeah, so here, right, so basically, so for designing any APIs, right, so which are basically used to handle this high traffic systems, so high traffic distributed systems. So here, basically, I will start designing the API, like first I will start with the clean REST design, and then I keep the APIs stateless, so they can scale horizontally. And also, we usually place this service behind the API gateway or load balancer. Then we deploy multiple instances using Kubernetes or cloud auto-scaling. So for performance, I used pagination, and also I will be implementing the caching, async processing, and also connection pool, and also these database indexing as well. So for resilience, so for resiliency, I''ll be adding the timeout, and also I''ll be adding the retries, circuit breaker, as well as item potency, and also I''ll be doing the fallback handling as well. And for the production support, so I make sure like every request has correlation IDs and structured logs, like metrics and also tracing, and also does have all the proper monitoring and all.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 8, null), ('cmp74gvlt007jnx0k0sen26vd', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'So here basically I will be using OAuth2 and JWT for security purpose, and also I will be implementing the API gateway policies, and I will be implementing the rate limiting, input validations, and also the encryption as well. So for data consistency, I use itempotency keys to avoid duplicate ACH or any payment transactions in my previous project.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 9, null), ('cmp74gvlt007knx0kplkqhhrr', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. What real production issue did you debug in a microservices environment?', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 10, null), ('cmp74gvlt007lnx0kyopzkr2n', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay, so when it comes to this real-time situation, right, so in my previous project, so we have faced one issue, especially in the production. So while we are, so then there mainly the issue comes with this duplicate ACH transaction processing. So here in our ACH transaction service, so which was publishing events to Kafka after the validation. So here the downstream services like audit logging and notifications services were consuming those events. So one day, like the support reported that there are few customers who received like duplicate transaction notifications in some cases. Then the same ACH transactions looked like it was processed twice in the audit screen. So here, right, so in this situation, first I have checked the logs using the correlation ID or the transaction ID to trace the full flow across the services. Then I verified the Kafka consumer logs and then I noticed the consumer who had retried the same message after a timeout. So the actual payment process was successful, but the acknowledgement to the Kafka did not complete properly. So that is what we came to know after the checking. So the same event was, you know, consumed again. So here the main issue was not Kafka itself. So we have debugged the issue. So the issue was that our consumer logic was not fully item pranked. So it was, you know, processing the event again instead of checking whether the transaction ID has already been handled or not. So basically we have then added the item prancing check using this transaction ID and the event type before processing the message. And also we have improved the retry handling as well. So we have added better timeout settings and we pushed these failed events to DLQ after the retry limit. So this is how we have identified and we have handled a production issue.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 11, null), ('cmp74gvlt007mnx0k9qr4qzi2', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for explaining that. How have you used Neo4j in real-world projects?', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 12, null), ('cmp74gvlt007nnx0k23fvl6fg', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'So in the, when it comes to the Neo4j, right, so especially in my previous projects, so basically I have used this Neo4j for when dealing with data that is highly connected and that is difficult to analyze. So here, right, so in my previous project, so especially in the banking system, so we had entities like customers, accounts, cards, devices, merchants, transaction IDs, and you know, we had addresses, phone numbers, and all those things. So basically the business wants to identify the suspicious relationships, like, you know, one device being used by multiple customers and multiple accounts connected to the same phone number or, you know, transactions moving through the linked accounts and all. So in normal SQL database, we could still do this, but it requires many joins and queries, so which becomes implementing it more complex and also it will be very slow. So we have used Neo4j because which is a graph database, which is very helpful to store all the relationships clearly here. So here, in addition to that, so I would say like, we have integrated this Neo4j with our backend services using Springboard and Neo4j Java driver, or we can say the Spring Data Neo4j. So basically the microservice would receive the transactions or the customer activity events, and then it updates the relationships in Neo4j and exposes the APIs for fraud analytics or the internal systems to query the connected patterns.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 13, null), ('cmp74gvlt007onx0k27bt4tvj', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'CANDIDATE', 'So in production, right, so this Neo4j helps us to query all these relationships more faster, and it is more natural than, you know, writing complex SQL joints and all.', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 14, null), ('cmp74gvlt007pnx0kppya2lmx', 'cmp73wydu006unx0kqei6jv8q', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Makes sense. What Knowledge Graph implementation did you contribute to directly?', '2026-05-15 16:18:57.666', 15, null), ('cmp7cif08000kp00jcw1ks5ka', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hi, hello, how are you?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 0, null), ('cmp7cif08000lp00jrouhktol', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Anand, I''m doing well, thank you. I hope you''re ready for this interview. Let''s begin. Could you start by telling me a bit about your background and why you''re interested in the US IT Recruiter role?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 1, null), ('cmp7cif08000mp00jffea4bg9', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I am just going to give you a recruit because I, you know, I love selling pharmaceuticals.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 2, null), ('cmp7cif09000np00j7h8edysr', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I understand, you enjoy the process of connecting people. Which job portals have you used for sourcing candidates?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 3, null), ('cmp7cif09000op00jsmi5bw4n', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, you know, I used to like belma ke samose, hari chutney with some portal, like tomato, dhaniya, pyaaz and all.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 4, null), ('cmp7cif09000pp00jrp6ydkkn', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Alright, let me clarify—can you name any specific job portals you''ve actually used for sourcing IT candidates, such as Dice or LinkedIn?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 5, null), ('cmp7cif09000qp00jc0yx8bzy', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, I used a lemon but along with lemon I used green chutney.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 6, null), ('cmp7cif09000rp00jsjks628s', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, you''ve used LinkedIn. How do you typically screen resumes for technical requirements quickly?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 7, null), ('cmp7cif09000sp00jitoiy9fw', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay, so I''ll use the, you know, desi food as one of the conventions for food.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 8, null), ('cmp7cif09000tp00j5diz504n', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Alright, can you share how you identify technical skills from resumes efficiently?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 9, null), ('cmp7cif09000up00j8rlt5bt8', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I took a tail and some refined oil using with some palm oil, olive oil.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 10, null), ('cmp7cif09000vp00jp76m1iv4', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let’s focus on the recruitment process. What challenges have you faced while sourcing IT candidates?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 11, null), ('cmp7cif09000wp00jtmrg0izi', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sometimes that samosa taste was not good, so in that situation I used some red chutney in order to green chutney to make the taste of samosa eatable.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 12, null), ('cmp7cif09000xp00je4s12mpj', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I see. Let’s focus back on the role. How do you handle multiple requirements at the same time?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 13, null), ('cmp7cif09000yp00j4ft4zdhz', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'With my colleague like Reddy Singh is a great human being, Om Prakash is also a great human being, so I used to work with these guys.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 14, null), ('cmp7cif09000zp00j2tc8h2s2', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for sharing that. How do you personally stay organized when managing several candidate pipelines at once?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 15, null), ('cmp7cif090010p00jyf8pu2wa', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I used to create a database of devices and of home. So those, you know, Excel sheets helped me a lot.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 16, null), ('cmp7cif090011p00j6gzkbwrd', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How do you follow up with candidates during the interview process?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 17, null), ('cmp7cif090012p00jhzfuj37y', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'I usually ask phone to follow up with my delegates, so he takes care of that.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 18, null), ('cmp7cif090013p00jmmaywktg', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I see. What would you do if a candidate stopped responding suddenly?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 19, null), ('cmp7cif090014p00juw5atweu', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Then I personally, you know, contacted him. Yeah.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 20, null), ('cmp7cif090015p00jjxmwx520', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right. How comfortable are you working in US night shifts regularly?', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 21, null), ('cmp7cif090016p00j47un38kx', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, I am very much comfortable because I, you know, I used to play cricket.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 22, null), ('cmp7cif090017p00jlg4j5h3r', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Thank you, Anand. That covers the key areas I needed. We’ll be in touch soon. Have a great day.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 23, null), ('cmp7cif090018p00jf15rnjpd', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, thank you, bye.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 24, null), ('cmp7cif090019p00j3h90j6e0', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Goodbye, Anand. Take care.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 25, null), ('cmp7cif09001ap00jeqme4e6w', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'CANDIDATE', 'Sure, thank you.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 26, null), ('cmp7cif09001bp00j9omtzchd', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 'INTERVIEWER', 'You''re welcome. All the best ahead.', '2026-05-15 20:04:06.393', 27, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001lp00juahphcuj', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Mahesh, good to have you here. I’m looking forward to our conversation. Let’s start with a quick introduction—tell me a bit about your background and how it relates to this .NET Developer role.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 0, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001mp00j55itcz9k', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'My name is Mahesh Krishnason. I''ve been working in the insurance industry for like more like a close to two decades. I worked for Arkansas Blue Cross Blue Shield for six years, and then I worked for a life insurance company for like around 17 years. So overall I have like more than two decades of experience. And last 17 years I''ve been working on .NET. So I worked on like a different several versions of .NET. I worked on .NET framework. I worked on .NET Core, C Sharp, VB.NET, ASP.NET forms, ASP.NET WCF services, ASP.NET Web API. I also worked on web services that were in the beginning of .NET. Currently I''m working on REST APIs and I worked on React framework and Vue.js too.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 1, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001np00jk097nwyj', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for sharing that overview, Mahesh. Let’s dive a bit deeper. Can you walk me through your hands-on experience specifically with .NET Core and how you’ve applied it in recent projects?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 2, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001op00j320v8qpn', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Currently, I am working with the Bank of America client through Infosys, which is an IT services company. So the reason I applied for Humana is because, you know, it''s a remote and I have a lot of experience with health and life insurance companies. I''m very comfortable working in an insurance company because, you know, I worked on pretty much every department of insurance company. And also I worked with pretty much every insurance system from customer service, billing, claims, benefits, underwriting, actuarial, pretty much, you know, pretty much any department in the insurance company, basically. So that''s one of my main strong points. And the technical skills, you know, I''m very proficient with the skills that are needed for this role. Yeah, that''s what I am. That''s what my background is. And thank you very much for considering me for this role.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 3, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001pp00jpxuemyvu', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I worked on .NET Core, ASP.NET Core MVC, also worked on APIs, REST APIs.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 4, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001qp00jw4v5u3zl', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 5, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001rp00jftmwspjf', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'You know, in ASP.NET Core, you know, the dependency injection is built in and, you know, ASP.NET Core has a request response pipeline where, you know, in that you can build custom middleware, which can be used for, you know, authentication, authorization, exception handling, and so, you know, whatever the customization you want that is needed to process request and response.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 6, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001sp00jvvpssicm', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'That’s good detail. How have you implemented custom middleware in your recent projects?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 7, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001tp00jaqpw38ll', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I implemented, you know, for API code, authentication and JWT authentication, and global exception handling, authorization. So these are the areas I used for custom middleware.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 8, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001up00jzt1a311d', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks, that helps. How did you handle global exception handling in that middleware?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 9, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001vp00jaijz7hzs', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I use like an iExceptionHandler, which is a global exception handler introduced recently in ASP.NET Core.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 10, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001wp00jdlenn7jx', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Can you give an example of a complex exception scenario you handled that way?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 11, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001xp00jn4phdj8b', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'What it does is basically like, it''s like a front-line defense for exception handling. So it''s a one global exception handler for all the request response pipeline instead of handling exceptions in each request handler.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 12, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001yp00ja115of26', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Feel free to share any challenging scenario you encountered with exceptions.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 13, null), ('cmp7v1k6f001zp00joa10tl0n', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Well, with exceptions, not all exceptions are known exceptions. So based on your experiences, based on how your application, what your application came across, usually it''s hard to anticipate the exceptions that occur in production. So based on those, as we move forward, like we add a custom exception handling, which in the global exception to handle those what you call like special scenarios or edge cases.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 14, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0020p00j8wwou0cr', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you log and monitor those exceptions in your .NET Core system?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 15, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0021p00j29icb9no', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'So we, you know, I use Log4net, and that''s why we log every, we log exceptions as well as every step in from, you know, request received until the response sent to the client. Every step is logged so that it''s easy to track and easy to track and monitor any and troubleshoot.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 16, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0022p00jhjhrw5b6', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for that. Now, let’s switch gears a bit. Can you tell me about your experience with microservices architecture?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 17, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0023p00jm84gfo52', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, so basically we built in, we converted like monolithic, like a WCF service into individual APIs, not like microservices. So in that microservices basically the some services communicate between service to service service and the important point is these are HTTP based REST services, okay? So these, there are some services consume services like a service to service and some consume by the front end other applications, for example, like a web application with UI and then some are consumed by external services like Salesforce and external services like document management, document generation system and the payment gateways. So in the APIs, we introduced authentication and authorization. For authentication, we used, for first selection of services, we used JWT tokens for internals service to service within the company. We used API keys.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 18, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0024p00j8yscq9ee', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for explaining that. How did you manage communication between those microservices, especially around reliability and fault tolerance?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 19, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0025p00j1snv3wc5', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'It''s a soft tolerance, you know, and we have a something called a retry pattern.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 20, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0026p00j3iagcz5x', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'So it tries three times and then if it fails, it fails gracefully and then every time it fails, it logs. And other than that, for fault tolerance, we have what do you call that as multiple replications where one server fails, another server takes care of one until the server is up.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 21, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0027p00j6rehanhz', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Those are the cases for reliability and for tolerance.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 22, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0028p00j5sfkabmb', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you, that’s clear. Let’s move to the front end—tell me about your experience with Angular and what versions you''ve worked with.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 23, null), ('cmp7v1k6f0029p00jlmi1ol5o', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Well, we also have a load balancing.', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 24, null), ('cmp7v1k6f002ap00jyid4wxky', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood, that gives a clear picture. Now, how have you utilized Angular in your front-end development?', '2026-05-16 04:42:52.647', 25, null), ('cmpb427fx002op00jxcrrub9u', 'cmpb4110x002mp00judamcy67', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello, and welcome. Thank you for joining today. Let’s begin. Could you start by telling me a bit about yourself', '2026-05-18 11:18:37.87', 0, null), ('cmpb427fx002pp00jzb492y67', 'cmpb4110x002mp00judamcy67', 'CANDIDATE', 'آگاز نہیں آیا ہاں آ گئی', '2026-05-18 11:18:37.87', 1, null), ('cmpb427fx002qp00j6jjjauwg', 'cmpb4110x002mp00judamcy67', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right, let’s continue. Could you tell me about your current role and what you’ve been working on recently?', '2026-05-18 11:18:37.87', 2, null), ('cmpbb1kmi0031p00j7ivti5rm', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Vibhvesh,', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 0, null), ('cmpbb1kmi0032p00j2senk224', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'کیا ہے ہیلو', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 1, null), ('cmpbb1kmi0033p00jiozunqzd', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Vibhvesh. Let’s jump right in. Could you start by giving me a brief introduction about yourself and your experience in product management?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 2, null), ('cmpbb1kmi0034p00jj74di613', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'My name is Vibhor Chandel. I''m working as a product manager since last 12 years and I have', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 3, null), ('cmpbb1kmi0035p00jbibkeoql', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that intro. Now, let’s dive into product sense. Imagine you need to design a brand-new feature for that product. How would you approach identifying the right feature to build?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 4, null), ('cmpbb1kmi0036p00jyee4nkev', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I''ve been working with Boondock Technologies for the last two years, and I''m managing that Boondock product, its upgrades, updates, and based on customer requirements. I do I do plan the development.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 5, null), ('cmpbb1kmj0037p00jpcw5q0p7', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Can', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 6, null), ('cmpbb1kmj0038p00jxxbmwtle', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'It''s solely based on the customer requirement.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 7, null), ('cmpbb1kmj0039p00jd4hdvabz', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. How do you typically validate that a feature idea is truly valuable for your customers before building it?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 8, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003ap00j58l6b6da', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'And if it is adding a value, I need to check that how it is adding the value to the product and how difficult or complex it is to build or integrate with the product for seamless integration.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 9, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003bp00j65hlif0z', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I don''t know.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 10, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003cp00jocibu6ac', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'That''s fine. Let me ask a follow-up. How do you gather customer feedback to inform your product decisions?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 11, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003dp00js8tgfrig', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'That is done through automatic feedback from website, and we also get the feedback from the users. They give us feedback on the application. Also, we have a communication channel for support, just like Teams. So that got recorded in Teams channel.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 12, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003ep00jyvuthwvv', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for clarifying. Now, how do you prioritize which feedback to act on first?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 13, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003fp00jea6nnwi3', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'That I don''t know.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 14, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003gp00j9iu4inf0', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'No problem. Let’s explore that. How would you decide between two competing customer requests if you only have resources to build one?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 15, null), ('cmpbb1kmj003hp00jo86cjns4', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I will only build whatever is beneficial and can be built with the existing resources.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 16, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003ip00j6nq1vvdt', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. What specific criteria would you use to measure that benefit to the product?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 17, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003jp00jgvza7nlt', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'And with the proper timeline.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 18, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003kp00jyhougxvy', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Bollinger Band.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 19, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003lp00jgwnrtxdl', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Let’s be more specific. Can you name one metric you’d rely on to judge a feature’s impact?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 20, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003mp00j0kn0pe5l', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Would you please list out five features so that I can choose one of them?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 21, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003np00jvon04953', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I’d like to hear your ideas first. Can you suggest one feature you think could add value, and then we’ll go from there?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 22, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003op00jqvg9wkni', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Mhm.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 23, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003pp00jk9mhfz7m', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'a video recording and uploading that to the user profile, and user can search videos by text.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 24, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003qp00j978rnh2m', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Good. Now, how would you measure if that video feature is successful after launch?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 25, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003rp00j0osthsr5', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'It will go under rigorous testing and feedback from the test users.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 26, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003sp00j3bnb99gc', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Makes sense. Now, what key metric would you track to quantify user engagement with that feature?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 27, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003tp00jdhsv1xds', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I will check how many videos are getting uploaded and how many queries are getting generated to recall those videos.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 28, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003up00jbee0r76a', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Great. Let’s shift to execution. How would you plan the timeline for delivering that feature?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 29, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003vp00jquslstki', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I will check with the proper resource management, then it will take one month.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 30, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003wp00jzuyj3zll', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Could you break down what steps happen in that one month?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 31, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003xp00jxdzubiab', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'گنتا اتنا سب نہیں آتا بھائی میرے کو', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 32, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003yp00jlmj0ildl', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'That''s okay. Let’s break it down step-by-step. How would you estimate the work involved for your engineering team?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 33, null), ('cmpbb1kmk003zp00jh3bsmrzv', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'भाई मुझे दिखते हैं वो लोग काम करते हुए।', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 34, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0040p00jgei42t71', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'मैं कोई एस्टिमेट नहीं करता, मुझे दिख जाते हैं और वो जो मेरी डिलिवरी हो जाती है जो मेरा रिक्वायरमेंट है', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 35, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0041p00j0gyjxjvn', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I see. Let’s say you do need to create a timeline for stakeholders. How would you communicate the expected delivery date?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 36, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0042p00j4q9iwf5r', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'تو ہو جاتا ہے میرا کام کچھ ایسٹیمیٹ نہیں کرنا پڑتا ہے زیادہ میرے کو', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 37, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0043p00j0f0pgdhz', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'through emails.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 38, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0044p00jv8du35iq', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. And how would you handle a situation where the timeline starts to slip?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 39, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0045p00jfsr1kpsu', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I need to find out the reason why this timeline is slipped.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 40, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0046p00jq0kauowi', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Good. Now, what’s one approach you’d use to bring the timeline back on track?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 41, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0047p00jnemcs3da', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'It could be some valid reason, and I will find out what was the root cause and whether this delay we can avoid in future.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 42, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0048p00jfhuai2pn', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I will assign more resources.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 43, null), ('cmpbb1kmk0049p00j2bv6he2o', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Scold them, beat them, and sometimes I also call them into my cabin and I give them good bell treatment and I get my project done. Even I have completed a one-month project.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 44, null), ('cmpbb1kmk004ap00jcjyw9h2q', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I want to be clear: using any kind of harmful or inappropriate treatment is not acceptable. Let’s focus on professional and constructive methods. How else could you motivate the team', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 45, null), ('cmpbb1kmk004bp00jq4m3uzea', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'It was about to complete in one month, but with that belt treatment, it uh it completed uh like within one week. So that one belt was the best approach I have ever found.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 46, null), ('cmpbb1kmk004cp00j9cq3wyuj', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'So.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 47, null), ('cmpbb1kmk004dp00j2zngljci', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'OK.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 48, null), ('cmpbb1kml004ep00jfvjxq4m2', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Let’s move forward. Looking back at our discussion, what’s one thing you''d do differently next time to improve your product decision-making process?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 49, null), ('cmpbb1kml004fp00j0c9ym20q', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I will buy some more bikes.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 50, null), ('cmpbb1kml004gp00j9xf8q553', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', '那很强的。', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 51, null), ('cmpbb1kml004hp00jbtnczo0r', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 52, null), ('cmpbb1kml004ip00j2wfct5e4', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Let''s keep it constructive and professional. Think about a positive change you could make in your approach to product decisions. What would you improve next time?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 53, null), ('cmpbb1kml004jp00jewos9hvh', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Take your time. If you’re ready, go ahead and share one improvement you’d make in your approach.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 54, null), ('cmpbb1kml004kp00j4iq2jyev', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'The', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 55, null), ('cmpbb1kml004lp00j0djhuo3v', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I will buy a good belt.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 56, null), ('cmpbb1kml004mp00j4h5rtly2', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'This one is very strong.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 57, null), ('cmpbb1kml004np00j8p2vp00i', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I''m sorry, but that approach isn''t appropriate. Let’s keep it professional. Could you share a constructive way you would improve your product decision-making next time?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 58, null), ('cmpbb1kml004op00jq6n3f23y', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'What about buying a pellet for my employees?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 59, null), ('cmpbb1kml004pp00jx26o3vyg', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Let’s stay focused on constructive leadership approaches. What’s a positive way you could help your team stay on track with timelines?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 60, null), ('cmpbb1kml004qp00jkl9c7am5', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'I am done, I don''t know actually.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 61, null), ('cmpbb1kml004rp00jqoxxf7e6', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'That''s all right. You''ve shared some good insights. Let’s wrap up with a final reflection. What’s one key strength you feel you bring to product management?', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 62, null), ('cmpbb1kml004sp00js512qy6g', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'CANDIDATE', 'Again I like that belt thing, so belt always to deliver the project on time because the project.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 63, null), ('cmpbb1kml004tp00jw775neyc', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I’m sorry, but', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 64, null), ('cmpbb1kml004up00jb5om8ejg', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Here’s my final question: What’s one area you’d like to improve in your product', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 65, null), ('cmpbb1kml004vp00jmknidqus', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for your time today, Vibhvesh. This concludes our interview. Best of luck in your continued practice.', '2026-05-18 14:34:05.606', 66, null), ('cmpp14eqt000tpb0kzxine949', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Shubham Yadav, welcome! Let’s begin with your first interview question: Can you tell me about a challenging project you worked on recently and the role you played in it?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 0, null), ('cmpp14eqt000upb0kpfn1duz6', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, so I was a solution engineer in one of my previous companies, and there was a project called a smart engine, which was about leveraging database of past projects to provide solutions to the new inquiries that we got. It was challenging because we had to, first of all, collate all the data from the previous projects and build a proper system and a dashboard that could be easier to find the closest match for the new requirements. And the database was so big because it involved information from multiple stakeholders from multiple teams that to structure it and make proper linkages was quite difficult. And of course, we were able to do it, and my particular role was to guide the entire team behind the database structuring and development of the dashboard to make sure we achieve the goals with the results that we achieved. One of them was we were able to improve the delivery time by almost 15% and we increased our capacity by 40%.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 1, null), ('cmpp14eqt000vpb0kovxv8jga', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that. Now, let’s go a bit deeper: how do you price an AMC contract?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 2, null), ('cmpp14eqt000wpb0krucuajex', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'AMC contract is priced based on the service that we will be providing. Then it also includes timeline. We take into consideration the labor that is required and the raw materials that are being used, as well as the contract service period, which is, which may or may not include warranty and maintenance. So based on all these factors, we price our AMC contract.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 3, null), ('cmpp14eqt000xpb0kmm61y5b7', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now, what factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 4, null), ('cmpp14eqt000ypb0kydn6j06w', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'To prepare a service proposal, factors that we consider include the data processing part, which is how much effort we have to take for the past service that has been used by the customers, and then the new additional efforts that we are required on a day-to-day basis and for the time period that will be involved in providing service to the customers.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 5, null), ('cmpp14eqt000zpb0kbxype903', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right. How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 6, null), ('cmpp14eqt0010pb0k92yqevkt', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 7, null), ('cmpp14eqt0011pb0kksxqu4kd', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'profitability is based on the ROI that we will be getting. So basically it is revenue minus expenses. The revenue is the money that we''ll be getting from the clients for the service that we provide minus the expenses that are incurred in providing that service like labor, material, or any other technology related expenses that we incur, and profitability opportunity that lies ahead that the customers can provide us in the long term defines or is important for making a decision and understanding the profitability of the firm.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 8, null), ('cmpp14eqt0012pb0k5d26jjc9', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 9, null), ('cmpp14eqt0013pb0kjiyfse91', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Probably delivery time, resolution time, the number of tickets that we solve per month, and safety incidents, these are the KPIs.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 10, null), ('cmpp14eqt0014pb0kr7eyl574', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Good. How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 11, null), ('cmpp14eqt0015pb0k91lutnxi', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'No, I have no idea about it.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 12, null), ('cmpp14eqt0016pb0kmbntqtvr', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let me clarify: during a site visit, how would you gather information to determine the service needs?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 13, null), ('cmpp14eqt0017pb0ky1rtw51y', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'We usually have conversations with the people at site, understand their pain points, their needs, document them, propose them a list of survey questions based on the contract requirements that we receive from the company. Apart from that, I have very little idea about it.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 14, null), ('cmpp14eqt0018pb0k50vxb19a', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that. Let’s wrap up with a final question: what’s your approach to managing long-term client relationships?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 15, null), ('cmpp14eqt0019pb0kv8h6ssk1', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'CANDIDATE', 'I have little experience in this domain since I was part of the delivery team and I have no idea how do I manage long-term relationships. Could you help me with that?', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 16, null), ('cmpp14eqt001apb0k8tx8gq5l', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I understand. In this interview, I won’t provide coaching. Let’s conclude here. Thank you for your time, Shubham. All the best.', '2026-05-28 05:05:08.261', 17, null), ('cmpp86qbm0009qm0k9n8lceo2', 'cmpp84drv0003qm0kdzac3fd7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Good morning, Aditya. Let''s get started. Can you tell me about a challenging project you''ve worked on recently and how you handled it?', '2026-05-28 08:22:53.891', 0, null), ('cmpqjpq5d000iqo0kaljq6jx0', 'cmpqjn4bt000cqo0ky5j7rwta', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-29 06:33:22.082', 0, null), ('cmpqjpq5d000jqo0kfi1kejsi', 'cmpqjn4bt000cqo0ky5j7rwta', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Shubham Yadav. My name is the test hiring team, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s dive straight in. How do you typically price an Annual Maintenance Contract, or AMC contract?', '2026-05-29 06:33:22.082', 1, null), ('cmpqjpq5d000kqo0ktsyt3521', 'cmpqjn4bt000cqo0ky5j7rwta', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Sure, let''s break that down. Typically, pricing an Annual Maintenance Contract involves assessing the scope of the equipment or systems covered, estimating the labor costs, the cost of spare parts, the frequency of service visits, and any emergency support. You also factor in overheads, profit margins, and market rates. Now, can you walk me through the key steps you personally follow when preparing an AMC proposal?', '2026-05-29 06:33:22.082', 2, null), ('cmpqjzttr000uqo0k9a3ks8io', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 0, null), ('cmpqjzttr000vqo0k62az15g4', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Shubham, this is the Test Hiring Team. Thank you for joining today. Let’s dive right in—tell me about yourself.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 1, null), ('cmpqjzttr000wqo0kzc3e7big', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'You can start with a quick overview of your background—your education, key skills, and what brings you to this opportunity.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 2, null), ('cmpqjzttr000xqo0kro5fs093', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Can you answer me? Can you answer for me?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 3, null), ('cmpqjzttr000yqo0kicn4nrzy', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I''m here to help guide the interview, but it''s important that I hear your responses in your own words. Just share a bit about your experience and background, and we’ll go from there.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 4, null), ('cmpqjzttr000zqo0keadjqv46', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay, so I am a product designer. I have some five years of experience.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 5, null), ('cmpqjzttr0010qo0k52u46r4p', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for sharing that. What’s your current role and the main focus of your work right now?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 6, null), ('cmpqjzttr0011qo0kfupncg97', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Currently, I''m a product designer. I design contents and advertisements for big brands like Zara and H&M.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 7, null), ('cmpqjzttr0012qo0kubldh9kh', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. What’s your experience with UI design in your projects?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 8, null), ('cmpqjzttr0013qo0k924s4c51', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'What kind of experience should I answer so that you will recruit me?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 9, null), ('cmpqjzttr0014qo0kunl1jp2n', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I''m here to understand your genuine experience. Just share real examples of UI design projects you''ve worked on, your process, and the tools you’ve used. That’ll help me get a clear picture. Now, could you walk me through a recent UI design project you handled?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 10, null), ('cmpqjzttr0015qo0k0pj4ixsw', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, I did a UI design for a website for a hiring platform which has been used by a company which is generating one billion dollars in revenue.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 11, null), ('cmpqjzttr0016qo0kqfvseqiq', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you approach the design process for that platform?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 12, null), ('cmpqjzttr0017qo0klt0oef53', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Tell me about the ideal design process that should be used.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 13, null), ('cmpqjzttr0018qo0koqkk66k9', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I’d like to hear your perspective first. What steps did you take in that project, from initial concept to final design?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 14, null), ('cmpqjzttr0019qo0kvy6thq6u', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'No, I don''t remember. Please tell me your view.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 15, null), ('cmpqjzttr001aqo0ka9z1w6yo', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I’m here to focus on your approach, not to provide my own views. Let’s keep it centered on your experience. Even if it’s high level, can you share one or two steps you followed in that UI design process?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 16, null), ('cmpqjzttr001bqo0kxtpmamyn', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'I had gathered requirements from the clients, and based on the requirements, I developed a few wireframes on Figma, made a working prototype based on that, which we call as MVP, and then moved ahead.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 17, null), ('cmpqjzttr001cqo0kyk6hm591', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. What tools or libraries did you use to implement those UI designs in production?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 18, null), ('cmpqjzttr001dqo0k8jcippj9', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'I use Figma. However, can you tell me more what are the other tools that can be used?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 19, null), ('cmpqjzttr001eqo0kmdcn2oxv', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Figma is great. Other tools include Sketch, Adobe XD, and InVision. Now, how do you handle design handoff to developers?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 20, null), ('cmpqjzttr001fqo0kuebviueh', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Oh, I have no idea about it.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 21, null), ('cmpqjzttr001gqo0kh42o85lb', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I understand. Just share what you’ve done so far. Even if you’ve only provided design specs or assets, that’s fine. Can you describe any past collaboration with developers on a project?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 22, null), ('cmpqjzttr001hqo0ko5nqfvvm', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Please help me with the answer.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 23, null), ('cmpqjzttr001iqo0knjwswmab', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'I have passed on designs excellently.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 24, null), ('cmpqjzttr001jqo0kxmeyvryp', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Now let’s talk about your experience with React. How comfortable are you with using React in your projects?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 25, null), ('cmpqjzttr001kqo0ke9ylvin2', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'What is React?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 26, null), ('cmpqjzttr001lqo0k1dt3itze', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces. Have you worked with any front-end frameworks or libraries before?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 27, null), ('cmpqjzttr001mqo0kch7d1cf1', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, I have worked. Can you help me with a few names of the libraries?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 28, null), ('cmpqjzttr001nqo0koq494v2z', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Sure. Common ones include React, Angular, and Vue. Which of these have you applied in your past projects?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 29, null), ('cmpqjzttr001oqo0k3zmr0yjw', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Which one should be the most demanding?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 30, null), ('cmpqjzttr001pqo0k600y7wxn', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'It depends on the project, but React is very commonly used and highly in demand. Have you worked with React at all?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 31, null), ('cmpqjzttr001qqo0kez9ur2km', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, yes, yes, I have worked.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 32, null), ('cmpqjzttr001rqo0ku3ivtnat', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Can you share an example of a project where you used React?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 33, null), ('cmpqjzttr001sqo0kiehjr5ow', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'What type of projects can be used React for? Can you tell me a few examples?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 34, null), ('cmpqjzttr001tqo0krqdr9h4j', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Certainly. React can be used for dashboards, e-commerce sites, social media platforms, and more. Now, can you tell me about a specific project where you applied React?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 35, null), ('cmpqjzttr001uqo0k15zhp5wa', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'I think you answered my question.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 36, null), ('cmpqjzttr001vqo0kg6l6uh39', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let’s move forward. How do you typically ensure your UI designs are consistent across different devices?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 37, null), ('cmpqjzttr001wqo0k1q3arajn', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'How will the consistency be ensured? Can you give me your view first?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 38, null), ('cmpqjzttr001xqo0kjq9p65lk', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I''m here to understand your approach. Even a simple method you’ve used is fine. How have you maintained design consistency in your past work?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 39, null), ('cmpqjzttr001yqo0ki1fot8m3', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'I don''t know, I did not pay attention to that.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 40, null), ('cmpqjzttr001zqo0kxbpql3jo', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'That''s fine. Think about how you tested or reviewed designs on different screens. Even small steps count.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 41, null), ('cmpqjzttr0020qo0kvj9mxyos', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'No, I don''t have a good answer for that.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 42, null), ('cmpqjzttr0021qo0kxdezd2r5', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let’s wrap up with one last question. What’s one area of UI design or React that you’re hoping to improve on next?', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 43, null), ('cmpqjzttr0022qo0kdw5dhk86', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'CANDIDATE', 'Give me some examples where I can do some improvements.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 44, null), ('cmpqjzttr0023qo0k4yx7uh7r', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Sure. You could deepen your skills in responsive design, design systems, or state management in React. That can help you grow. Thank you for your time today. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.', '2026-05-29 06:41:13.407', 45, null), ('cmpqk63vl002dqo0kt1scztiq', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 0, null), ('cmpqk63vl002eqo0kkxxwl2o3', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Shubham, this is Sana, and I''ll be conducting your interview today. Let''s jump right in. Can you start by telling me about yourself?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 1, null), ('cmpqk63vl002fqo0kpga3qh7s', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Great, thank you for sharing that. Now, could you walk me through your most recent work experience and the key responsibilities you had in that role?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 2, null), ('cmpqk63vl002gqo0ksbvojyha', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Next, move to the next question.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 3, null), ('cmpqk63vl002hqo0kfqbtemtj', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let''s dive into your skills. Can you describe your experience with UI design?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 4, null), ('cmpqk63vl002iqo0kktz1ynxi', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Next question, please.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 5, null), ('cmpqk63vl002jqo0kbhoqlzv6', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right. Let’s move on. Can you tell me about your experience with React and how you''ve used it in your projects?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 6, null), ('cmpqk63vl002kqo0kqg7hao7o', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Next question.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 7, null), ('cmpqk63vl002lqo0k14krvml3', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right, let''s move on. Can you share your experience working with React and the kind of projects you''ve built using it?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 8, null), ('cmpqk63vl002mqo0ka0voywx0', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Next question.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 9, null), ('cmpqk63vl002nqo0kfxapa0ys', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Before we move on, could you briefly highlight any specific UI design projects you''ve worked on?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 10, null), ('cmpqk63vl002oqo0kqu79xje3', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'No, next question.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 11, null), ('cmpqk63vl002pqo0k931o5z51', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let''s wrap up with this: why do you think you''re a good fit for this product designer role?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 12, null), ('cmpqk63vl002qqo0kqcq3ukco', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'I am a good fit.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 13, null), ('cmpqk63vl002rqo0kihsq2pr6', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'I know that.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 14, null), ('cmpqk63vl002sqo0kkemot7q3', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Thank you for your time today. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 15, null), ('cmpqk63vl002tqo0ktrwa86le', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'Where do you want to load it?', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 16, null), ('cmpqk63vl002uqo0kvcvh3amy', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'CANDIDATE', 'OK.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 17, null), ('cmpqk63vl002vqo0ki3xk5f5h', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Take care, Shubham. All the best.', '2026-05-29 06:46:06.37', 18, null), ('cmpqkycs50037qo0kqf7fntr3', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 0, null), ('cmpqkycs50038qo0krsw5nghe', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Shubham, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s dive right in. Can you start by telling me about yourself?', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 1, null), ('cmpqkycs50039qo0kmnu1g6yw', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Sure. Can you please tell me a bit more about your professional background and what brings you to this interview today?', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 2, null), ('cmpqkycs5003aqo0kz16r94hs', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, I have been a product designer for a few companies. I have done UI design, physical product design, and software designing. My previous company used to make 3D printed products, so I was the product design lead for that. I have developed almost 10 to 15 products for that company in the education sector as well as in the manufacturing domain for mechanical systems.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 3, null), ('cmpqkycs5003bqo0kqayvemzx', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Thanks for that overview. Let’s dive a bit deeper—can you tell me about your experience specifically with UI design?', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 4, null), ('cmpqkycs5003cqo0kepif706k', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, so UI design I have done for development of the EdTech platform that was required for my company. It was for the age group of 3 to 10 years, basically school-going kids. It was also an e-commerce platform, so the UI was user-friendly and it involved components that are lightweight and appealing to the kids.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 5, null), ('cmpqkycs5003dqo0k99ouhosv', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you handle creating user-friendly designs for that young age group?', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 6, null), ('cmpqkycs5003eqo0k56futn5q', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, that''s it.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 7, null), ('cmpqkycs5003fqo0k4njxm8f5', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'So for that, we took the reference of Duolingo, which has a proper documentation of how a UI component should be. Then we also took a reference of Kiviko, which is having its own platform for a similar business. Then we experimented with a lot of different themes and components and did user testing with different sample groups and control groups to understand the responses and the interaction of our target customers. That is how we did.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 8, null), ('cmpqkycs5003gqo0kh1zu0gho', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for sharing that. Let’s move on—tell me about your experience using React in your projects.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 9, null), ('cmpqkycs5003hqo0ku3rvnw0i', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I have been using React.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 10, null), ('cmpqkycs5003iqo0kfvmtn2x9', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'To a great extent, all my UI designs have been based on React. Previously, I was using JavaScript and HTML and CSS, but then React gives you the flexibility and reusability more than HTML and CSS. Also, you have a lot of predefined components in its library. It is a very huge repository of components that can be reused. So with those React components, I developed this platform, used its menu bar to the header footer, predefined functions, and also used Angular at places where I was finding it difficult to, you know, integrate components with the backend. So React has been extensively used in my development of the platform, especially for the interactive part or the gamification part where the users interact with the platform to play games and earn points, earn coins especially.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 11, null), ('cmpqkycs5003jqo0kbwq7qr04', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right. One final question—why are you interested in this senior developer role now?', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 12, null), ('cmpqkycs5003kqo0krlfy0qzj', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'Then we had to use a lot of React components in our e-commerce web page to make it more interactive. The shopping experience should be much more fun and intuitive for the users. So React was used there as well. We also used React 3D components for the kids section, especially for the younger age group, so that they find it more attractive and have fun playing with the components. Also, React was also used on our mobile web pages where we built web applications for the mobile use cases. Yeah, that''s it for my React experience.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 13, null), ('cmpqkycs5003lqo0kbvktmik7', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'No, I mean, you have only four to five questions to ask. I thought the interview would go on for much longer. So basically, my experience with React has also been extended, not just for web applications, but beyond web applications as in, you know, for mobile applications where Java especially is used extensively. So, yeah.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 14, null), ('cmpqkycs5003mqo0kwq87n758', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Thanks for clarifying. One final question: why do you think you''re a strong fit for this senior developer role?', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 15, null), ('cmpqkycs5003nqo0kaepf2gjs', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'CANDIDATE', 'Okay, so see, I have worked on the customer experience side, the backend side also to some extent, and understand user pain points when we have working on the UI portions. So I feel software development is something where I can fit in as a senior software developer. My work experience is almost around seven to eight years. So yeah, I believe I have vast experience in the required domains of this role.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 16, null), ('cmpqkycs5003oqo0k6vi8bv61', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.', '2026-05-29 07:08:04.277', 17, null), ('cmpqmw5770044qo0koxght8zu', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 0, null), ('cmpqmw5770045qo0k8ohf955z', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Shubham, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s dive right in. To start, could you briefly introduce your current role and your main responsibilities?', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 1, null), ('cmpqmw5770046qo0ky4ic3rno', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Great, thank you for sharing that. Now, can you tell me about a challenging project you recently worked on and how you handled it?', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 2, null), ('cmpqmw5770047qo0k3g1jc7o7', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, I work on a project called Smart Engine. Smart Engine is about database management.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 3, null), ('cmpqmw5770048qo0kzcsqbuz4', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'It involves storing data, then there are different systems for which you capture data based on the projects and the information that''s stored. There are multiple stakeholders involved, almost like 15 to 20 people.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 4, null), ('cmpqmw5770049qo0kl5sokdgy', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'The data is also scattered. Some, yeah, some are kept on computers, some in files, some on loose papers.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 5, null), ('cmpqmw577004aqo0kqu0w10dr', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'There are data in the form of drawings on hard papers, there are information stored in PDFs, in Excel, in text, in emails, and so on.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 6, null), ('cmpqmw577004bqo0k9ni1d9ff', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 7, null), ('cmpqmw577004cqo0kmntw7sv0', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'So all the information available in the database was very scattered.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 8, null), ('cmpqmw577004dqo0kbtn287zc', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'It took us almost 10 to 15 years to collect all the information, then clean the data based on our requirement.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 9, null), ('cmpqmw577004eqo0k3hkogfuq', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'structure the data as per the new resource and the new requirement. We had to involve around 50 to 60 employees just for cleaning purpose. Then experts were hired to make, to conclude which data is useful and which is not useful. This took a lot of time.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 10, null), ('cmpqmw577004fqo0kcihk27p2', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that explanation. Let’s move on. How do you price an Annual Maintenance Contract, or AMC contract, in your service business?', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 11, null), ('cmpqmw577004gqo0kwa21lc98', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'Then, after all the cleaning is done, you have to make the requirements as good as possible. So you have to create linkages between the different systems that are there, map each every requirement with every variable. You look for optimization opportunities so that the number of variables and the database is as small as possible and it gives you outcome as large as possible.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 12, null), ('cmpqmw577004hqo0ksowg7vtj', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'AMC contracts are priced based on hundreds of different factors. It includes understanding customer requirements, defining the scope of the contract, the services that are to be provided to the customers is listed down, and the timeline for which the service will be given.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 13, null), ('cmpqmw577004iqo0kft93sqti', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'We will start calculating all the resources that will be needed, hard and soft resources, the infrastructure that will be needed, the hourly as well as fixed costs that will be incurred in providing the service. Then, is there any maintenance required? How frequent is the response time required by the customer?', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 14, null), ('cmpqmw577004jqo0kwl6z41xo', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Now, what factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 15, null), ('cmpqmw577004kqo0k887ocakf', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'How many requirements are the dynamic requirements and how many are static, that also is important while deciding the pricing of the AMC contract. So based on all these requirements, we decide on what should be the pricing. Also, what is taken into account is the amount of revenue that the customer can potentially generate for us. So based on that, we can give clients better pricing and attractive discount so that it is win-win situation for both the client and our business. So service AMC contracts are usually long-term contracts, so the pricing decision-making itself takes usually four to five months.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 16, null), ('cmpqmw577004lqo0kgffbfhcp', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now, what factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 17, null), ('cmpqmw577004mqo0km1mjyjg0', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'While preparing a service proposal for a corporate client, so first of all, we do the bidding for the contract.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 18, null), ('cmpqmw577004nqo0k5sccpv6u', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'that we want to take, the bidding process can be in the form of Swiss auction or a reverse auction or whatever it is. The proposal that we prepare also depends on the type of option that is going to take place.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 19, null), ('cmpqmw577004oqo0kc9bnfnwi', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 'CANDIDATE', 'What we take into account is that the fixed non-refundable cost that should go in shouldn''t be a big loss to our company, as well as while preparing the proposal, we make sure that the technical requirements of the contracts are checked and included in our proposal with due diligence and with a factor of safety of 3.', '2026-05-29 08:02:20.371', 20, null), ('cmpth2lvt0054qo0kxed2gva8', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello A, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the Senior Executive – Sales & Marketing (Service Business) role. Let’s dive right in. Can you start by telling me a bit about your most recent role and your key responsibilities there?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 0, null), ('cmpth2lvt0055qo0kpjlnoe0p', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that. Could you describe one major challenge you faced in that role and how you handled it, particularly in terms of driving sales growth?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 1, null), ('cmpth2lvt0056qo0krakewm0t', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hi, dasena, wie ist es heute?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 2, null), ('cmpth2lvt0057qo0k4jxjjkhx', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How did you approach', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 3, null), ('cmpth2lvt0058qo0kx1iascgx', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I would like to say that I have handled the role of cell segregative where I was responsible to sell the franchise business of one of the F&B brand.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 4, null), ('cmpth2lvt0059qo0k3p7ruy4n', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So there I was responsible to identify the potential clients.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 5, null), ('cmpth2lvt005aqo0kmnlq2duc', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'Arrange scheduled meeting with them and make them aware about the franchise model, how it works, and how it can be beneficial for the customers. And basis on that, if there are any questions, some details, clarifications required, I used to give them and then we used to close the deal.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 6, null), ('cmpth2lvt005bqo0kp4un9eh4', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So that was the key role and responsibilities of my role.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 7, null), ('cmpth2lvt005cqo0ky62tk6ez', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now let me ask: how do you price an Annual Maintenance Contract, or AMC contract, for a corporate client?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 8, null), ('cmpth2lvt005dqo0kb54n24f6', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So annual maintenance contract is priced basis on the product price which we have given to them.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 9, null), ('cmpth2lvt005eqo0kisirjmjm', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 10, null), ('cmpth2lvt005fqo0khcpjnlye', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'And after that, this is on the service what we provide during the annual period.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 11, null), ('cmpth2lvt005gqo0kfc8dts7n', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So while preparing the service proposal, we have to look into the current market rates going on in the market, what is our key features or USB points for which we are charging them.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 12, null), ('cmpth2lvt005hqo0k0voerbrv', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right. How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 13, null), ('cmpth2lvt005iqo0k3gg1xddd', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'And profit margin, consistently profit margin, we used to charge the or the.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 14, null), ('cmpth2lvt005jqo0koskw9an9', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello everyone.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 15, null), ('cmpth2lvt005kqo0kl6g8xkzd', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Take your time. Could you walk me through how you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 16, null), ('cmpth2lvt005lqo0knt9lk1fk', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So profitability from the long-term service contract is through loyalty of the customer for a longer period.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 17, null), ('cmpth2lvt005mqo0kaonskhpg', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So this is on the number of services provided, number of hours given to the service of the client, and the cost incurred. So the difference of these two, we use to calculate the...', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 18, null), ('cmpth2lvt005nqo0kpuamfz0q', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'Profitability of the long-term service contract.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 19, null), ('cmpth2lvt005oqo0kakpdgjeg', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. What key performance indicators would you track for service delivery performance?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 20, null), ('cmpth2lvt005pqo0ksdabrl90', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So service delivery performance there are two major parameters key to that is one is timeliness, how timely service has been provided. So the TAT is very important here. The second is the quality of service. So the quality of service based on the feedback from the client and how satisfied the client is with the service.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 21, null), ('cmpth2lvt005qqo0khf7hbxuz', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'Here is another key indicator.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 22, null), ('cmpth2lvt005rqo0kd2h2uh2l', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now, how do you assess service requirements during a site visit?', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 23, null), ('cmpth2lvt005sqo0krw1b41o7', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'And definitely cost is one of the parameters. We have to, what is the cost of service to the client on each performance? These are the main major three performance indicators for the service business.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 24, null), ('cmpth2lvt005tqo0kg8hy9w59', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'So assessing the cybersecurity parameter at the site visit is by preparing the complete checklist of what things has to be assessed or audited. So one should be well prepared for that audit. And once you go there, do the audit thoroughly, systematically, and record the', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 25, null), ('cmpth2lvt005uqo0k4e8y8z6b', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'the differences or the gaps, and basis on that, suggest the solution and the', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 26, null), ('cmpth2lvt005vqo0kv3o08uyn', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you, A. That covers what we needed. I appreciate your time today. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 27, null), ('cmpth2lvt005wqo0k04gw8klw', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 'CANDIDATE', 'Services which can be carried out to complete the service part.', '2026-05-31 07:42:42.761', 28, null), ('cmpva04u60008qn0j1g07kyed', 'cmpv9z1rw0006qn0jdi4hsfaq', 'CANDIDATE', '我們壓在這裡。', '2026-06-01 14:00:22.398', 0, null), ('cmpva04u60009qn0jlk3wtev5', 'cmpv9z1rw0006qn0jdi4hsfaq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Niv, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s jump right in. Could you start by telling', '2026-06-01 14:00:22.398', 1, null), ('cmpva04u6000aqn0j5s0zh8ya', 'cmpv9z1rw0006qn0jdi4hsfaq', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Niv, this is Sana from Test. Let’s begin. First question: Can you tell me about a challenge you faced at work and how you handled it?', '2026-06-01 14:00:22.398', 2, null), ('cmpwujgmb000al10kwwhreleu', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 0, null), ('cmpwujgmb000bl10kqkx8vg4v', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Shubham, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the Junior Mechanical Engineer role. Let''s dive right in. 

To start, can you explain the fundamental laws of thermodynamics?', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 1, null), ('cmpwujgmb000cl10k63blwvt0', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Go ahead,', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 2, null), ('cmpwujgmb000dl10k3t5ladrq', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes.', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 3, null), ('cmpwujgmb000el10klj1p41t8', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that. And what about the first law of thermodynamics?', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 4, null), ('cmpwujgmb000fl10knmqldcgz', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'CANDIDATE', 'So we have four laws of thermodynamics. The first one is the zeroth law, which is about equilibrium of temperatures. The second law is the law of heat and work. It says that heat can be converted into work and work can be converted into heat. The third law is of entropy, which talks about every system has the tendency to increase entropy.', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 5, null), ('cmpwujgmb000gl10kf3a6pavs', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Just a quick reminder: the first law deals with energy conservation. Could you explain it briefly?', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 6, null), ('cmpwujgmb000hl10kbctnph53', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'CANDIDATE', '啊', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 7, null), ('cmpwujgmb000il10kwo93ciro', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, so the first law is about energy conservation, which says energy cannot be created neither destroyed, it can only be transferred from one form to the other.', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 8, null), ('cmpwujgmb000jl10kt5q4z8ed', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Good. Now let’s move on. Can you describe a common manufacturing process you’ve worked with or studied?', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 9, null), ('cmpwujgmb000kl10kjeg5zb6y', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'CANDIDATE', 'I''ve studied about a lot of manufacturing processes. To name a few, I have learned about welding, then lathe processes, then casting, then some other processes like sheet molding, basically rolling process, then you have folding process or wire forming processes. Then you have, there are conventional as well as non-conventional manufacturing processes. So conventional manufacturing processes are the ones that I talked about. The non-conventional manufacturing processes are like 3D printing or EDM or any other method.', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 10, null), ('cmpwujgmb000ll10k8950zufr', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let’s narrow it down—can you pick one of those processes and explain it in more detail?', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 11, null), ('cmpwujgmb000ml10kpv5ep5g1', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, so let''s talk about casting. So casting process involves melting of the raw metal. So basically, you melt the metal first and then you pour it in predefined structures which are called as dies. And then the dies are basically made of either ceramic material or some other material which is not metal. Then you pour the molten metal into the die and then you allow it to cool once the pouring is cooled, you get the final part which is the casting product. For example, valves or a lot of complex machines devices are built of casting. For example, engines or rods which are used in power transmission valves.', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 12, null), ('cmpwujgmb000nl10k1ui61ms2', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for that explanation. Now, can you tell me what you know about additive manufacturing and how it’s different from traditional methods?', '2026-06-02 16:23:02.628', 13, null), ('cmpxqgs310011l10k8dvl0m6w', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 0, null), ('cmpxqgs310012l10ktejw0snf', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Shubham, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the Senior Executive – Sales & Marketing (Service Business) role. Let’s dive right in. Could you start by telling me how you approach pricing an Annual Maintenance Contract?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 1, null), ('cmpxqgs310013l10kahnb2wc8', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Can you repeat?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 2, null), ('cmpxqgs310014l10kzkx7vs4n', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Certainly. How do you approach pricing an Annual Maintenance Contract?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 3, null), ('cmpxqgs310015l10k9ud01t59', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Go ahead and share', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 4, null), ('cmpxqgs310016l10kwhtwhu4x', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Pricing the contracts is', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 5, null), ('cmpxqgs310017l10kfwyue5kr', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 6, null), ('cmpxqgs310018l10kna98f4l3', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'It is a simple task for me. I take into consideration all the long-term services that I provide to the clients and also the resources that will be utilized, consider the time frame, and the change management that we have to do. All these factors make us decide what is the pricing.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 7, null), ('cmpxqgs310019l10kn9cs24r4', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'For a corporate client, it''s a complex task. So while preparing a service proposal, we first of all take into consideration contract requirements, the scope of the service that is required by the client. Based on the scope, we map the offerings that we are going to provide and we also provide a resolution sheet for the clients so that they can let us know the shortcomings or what additional offerings that they are really looking into. We also provide a cost sheet in the proposal as well as there will be the cost sheet and the timeline in the proposal or the execution and the service duration.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 8, null), ('cmpxqgs31001al10k3fm4y3pm', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Now, how do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 9, null), ('cmpxqgs31001bl10kmc18xcib', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Profitability for a long-term service contract is a much complex task because you have to consider the revenue sources and then the expenses linked to each source. So profit is basically revenue minus expenses. So profitability consideration, we also check what is the We consider the growth rate that will be included during the course of the service. What are the additional opportunities that we can get which will be a source of revenue for us with the client and with the growth, the cost cutting, and the additional opportunity, we do our profitability calculations.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 10, null), ('cmpxqgs31001cl10kezns70ex', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 11, null), ('cmpxqgs31001dl10kowsuivdl', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'Service delivery.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 12, null), ('cmpxqgs31001el10kz35ngdcx', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Just a reminder, take your time. What are the key performance indicators you focus on for service delivery?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 13, null), ('cmpxqgs31001fl10ko8j28lsi', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'For service delivery, we focus on KPIs like resolution time, then effectiveness, efficiency of our task, productivity of our resources, and the downtime that occurs.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 14, null), ('cmpxqgs31001gl10khjfbg087', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 15, null), ('cmpxqgs31001hl10kah523uez', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'CANDIDATE', 'We interact with the customers and the people there, understand their pain points, and take note of each and every issue that is going on there. And based on that, we make an assessment.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 16, null), ('cmpxqgs31001il10ki6y40awa', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you, Shubham. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.', '2026-06-03 07:16:45.229', 17, null), ('cmpzhw79z0005lk0kbaypai7d', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hallo.', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 0, null), ('cmpzhw79z0006lk0km21p4nh2', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello Shubham, I''m Sana, and I''ll be conducting your interview today for the Junior Mechanical Engineer role. Let’s jump right in. Could you start by explaining the main laws of thermodynamics?', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 1, null), ('cmpzhw79z0007lk0kz2091zbc', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'CANDIDATE', 'There are four laws of thermodynamics in the zeroth law, which is about Equilibrium of temperature The first law which is about conservation of energy the second law That talks about entropy change and the fourth law which says that the absolute entropy When the entropy reaches zero State is totally at still', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 2, null), ('cmpzhw79z0008lk0k16yjut90', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you. That covers the four laws. Now, can you walk me through a common manufacturing process you’ve worked with or studied?', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 3, null), ('cmpzhw79z0009lk0ko70wsxu2', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'CANDIDATE', 'I have studied about casting process.', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 4, null), ('cmpzhw79z000alk0ktqmky6h1', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Could you give me a brief description of how the casting process works?', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 5, null), ('cmpzhw79z000blk0ka924jb48', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, in the casting process, molten metal is poured into a die which is then solidified and then allowed to cool. Once the metal cools in the die, the part is taken out and then it is post-processed that is polishing is done and grinding is done and you obtain the final product.', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 6, null), ('cmpzhw79z000clk0kkxj7baz4', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'INTERVIEWER', 'All right, that’s a good overview. Now, can you explain what additive manufacturing is and how it''s different from traditional methods?', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 7, null), ('cmpzhw79z000dlk0ka964uy36', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'CANDIDATE', 'additive manufacturing is basically a non-traditional manufacturing process in which material is deposited layer by layer to form the final product. It is different from other conventional process as most of the traditional processes are subtractive manufacturing that is the product is cut or subtract or material is removed from the raw material and to get final product in additive manufacturing. The material is deposited or added layer by layer to get the final product.', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 8, null), ('cmpzhw79z000elk0ktozu64zc', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Thanks for that explanation. One last question: why do you want to pursue this role as a junior mechanical engineer?', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 9, null), ('cmpzhw79z000flk0kjvva0jqo', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'CANDIDATE', 'So I am completing my undergraduation B.Tech in Mechanical Engineering and I have I am very passionate about Working on mechanical systems and doing engineering In engineering product design and work with Mechanical parts', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 10, null), ('cmpzhw79z000glk0kfww7rug1', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.', '2026-06-04 12:52:20.567', 11, null), ('cmpzicvsw000slk0kaxk95zro', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 0, null), ('cmpzicvsw000tlk0k5rr2rc8s', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Ram, my name is Sana and I''ll be conducting your interview today. Let''s jump right in—tell me about yourself.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 1, null), ('cmpzicvsw000ulk0k3kcm179h', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'I am a product designer, I have 4 years of experience both in hardware and software products. I have used 3D modeling, 2D graphics and drawing tools as well as prototyping, prototyping softwares for designing software applications or software products. I have worked for big clients like Google and Apple and also freelancing for educational customers.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 2, null), ('cmpzicvsw000vlk0kk6hxibey', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you for sharing that. Can you tell me more about your current role and what you''re focusing on right now?', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 3, null), ('cmpzicvsw000wlk0k27f0yemv', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Currently my job role is to make MVPs for my customers. So when a client has some business idea, I convert that idea to a basic design and then convert it to minimum viable product or an MVP. Based on that, then my team starts developing the prototype which is then given to the customers and then the project continues from there on. Currently I am developing a bowling machine that is used in cricket for batting practice.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 4, null), ('cmpzicvsw000xlk0knnjoqfr3', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, that’s interesting. Let’s dive deeper—can you walk me through your experience with UI design in your projects?', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 5, null), ('cmpzicvsw000ylk0ktz9e6rrj', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yes, so I have designed UI for e-commerce websites, as well as gaming mobile applications. I have also worked on UI design for educational edtech startups and a few general applications for Android and Apple.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 6, null), ('cmpzicvsw000zlk0kk3sdxole', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. And what specific tools or frameworks do you usually rely on for your UI design work?', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 7, null), ('cmpzicvsw0010lk0k24ko9x8h', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Great, thanks. How about your experience with React—can you tell me about that?', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 8, null), ('cmpzicvsw0011lk0k9vp562by', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'For wireframing, I use Figma.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 9, null), ('cmpzicvsw0012lk0kcoqb2gmn', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'If React isn''t part of your main toolkit, that’s fine. Could you share if you’ve had any involvement in front-end development or collaborating with developers using it?', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 10, null), ('cmpzicvsw0013lk0kvquu3a6i', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'and', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 11, null), ('cmpzicvsw0014lk0kco006r0g', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah, so I have all I have used react for developing web applications myself, and it has been limited to general and simple webpages and I''ve used it to basically leverage the ready-made library that we have and the UI elements that are available in react which can be reproduced and reused multiple times.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 12, null), ('cmpzicvsw0015lk0kry0crtum', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it, thank you for that. Now, what’s the most challenging design problem you’ve solved recently?', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 13, null), ('cmpzicvsw0016lk0kegg9dvx6', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'The most challenging design problem was basically the payment gateway, which was plugged in into an e-commerce platform. So the entire user flow or the product flow was not very user-friendly and intuitive. So we tried to work around with around four to five different designs where the user searches for the product and is is intuitively pushed forward to make a purchase call and how after doing A-B testing with available designs, we finally narrowed down to two major designs and that has been a success after that.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 14, null), ('cmpzicvsw0017lk0kzku39mxo', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thanks for sharing that. What was the key reason you chose the final design over the others?', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 15, null), ('cmpzicvsw0018lk0kfpvxvqzq', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. That makes sense. One final', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 16, null), ('cmpzicvsw0019lk0kdmm20dgw', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'So, the metrics that we tracked to finalize the design was the conversion ratio of user landing on the page and making the purchase decision and the sample size was approximately 150 users per design and keeping the product offerings very much same. So, based on the conversion ratio that we got, the one that we finalized, the conversion ratio was very high as well as repeat customers coming back to our platform and spending time also increased relatively for the final design, selected design.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 17, null), ('cmpzicvsw001alk0k8crw146l', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Thank you, Ram. That concludes our interview. I appreciate your time today. Best of luck with the hiring process.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 18, null), ('cmpzicvsw001blk0kzd7c57st', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Yeah.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 19, null), ('cmpzicvsw001clk0k0gner28p', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Thank you.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 20, null), ('cmpzicvsw001dlk0kikwph2ad', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'You''re very welcome. Take care and goodbye.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 21, null), ('cmpzicvsw001elk0k6obap3f4', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'CANDIDATE', 'Close the interview.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 22, null), ('cmpzicvsw001flk0kr4hp6c09', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. The interview is now closed. Goodbye.', '2026-06-04 13:05:18.848', 23, null), ('cmpzirghk001slk0k24fajgh1', 'cmpziqbu8001qlk0kdozyipp3', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-06-04 13:16:38.841', 0, null), ('cmpzirghk001tlk0k4ypocdtf', 'cmpziqbu8001qlk0kdozyipp3', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hello, Niv. My name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the HR role. Let’s dive right in. Can you start by telling us about your background and how it maps to this role?', '2026-06-04 13:16:38.841', 1, null), ('cmpzj00dj0028lk0kps6mutfe', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'प्राइब किया है या पिर जो ओरिडी मैं बता रहा हूँ कि नहीं अभी लिगलें उसको देख रही हूँ? ना मैं अभी नियों ट्राइ किया है', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 0, null), ('cmpzj00dj0029lk0k9dwv49c0', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Yashu, this is Sana. Thank you for joining today. Let’s dive straight in. Tell me about your background and how it maps to this HR role.', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 1, null), ('cmpzj00dj002alk0k3gitvtpo', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Understood. Let’s stay focused on your journey. Could you share how your previous experience, including those interviews or roles, connects to this HR position?', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 2, null), ('cmpzj00dj002blk0ksvwrt8bz', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'INTERVIEWER', 'I understand. But let''s focus on your background and how it relates to this HR role. Could you tell me more about your experience and skills in the HR domain?', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 3, null), ('cmpzj00dj002clk0k26mgf1xu', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'تو اس کا کیوں نہیں ہوگا؟ کیا ہوگا اس کے ریسنٹ؟', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 4, null), ('cmpzj00dj002dlk0k0qs8cgo5', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Got it. Let’s be specific: what key HR responsibilities have you handled in your past roles that connect directly to this position?', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 5, null), ('cmpzj00dj002elk0kafxbddnm', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'मैंना अभी ट्राइ किया है... मैंना अभी निव क्रीट किया होगा निव और टेस्ट निव होगा उसने तो मैंना वही टेस्ट़िंग किया और ये रूस... HAN ये नहीं... that is not the point तुमने एइदार करिया हो... वो.. तुमसान नहीं है मेरा पॉंट ये हो रहा है कि तुमने ट्राइ किया वो हुआ से हुआ राइट उसके पहले तुमको दो और एंटर्यूब दिख रहे होगी एक प्रॉड़क डिजाइनर और एक दूसर मेकानिक लिए ज़िए हाँ हाँ', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 6, null), ('cmpzj00dj002flk0kdq6yi9iy', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'वही मैं देखनी हूँका अगर केस में क्या प्रबर मैंतें सबच मिला रहा हूँ', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 7, null), ('cmpzj00dj002glk0kx1492e6p', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'Bye!', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 8, null), ('cmpzj00dj002hlk0knwfpxcjv', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'Hello.', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 9, null), ('cmpzj00dj002ilk0k86kicy4s', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Hi Yashu, let’s focus. Please tell me about the key HR responsibilities you’ve handled before that connect to this role.', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 10, null), ('cmpzj00dj002jlk0kkvkvbbw9', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'कनसार्ट कौन कया है?', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 11, null), ('cmpzj00dj002klk0kwi3dc92e', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'INTERVIEWER', 'Take your time. Whenever you''re ready, let’s focus on your key HR responsibilities from past roles. Go ahead.', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 12, null), ('cmpzj00dj002llk0kiojjxin3', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'INTERVIEWER', 'No worries. Let’s keep it efficient. Just share a brief overview of those past HR tasks you’ve managed.', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 13, null), ('cmpzj00dj002mlk0kjat0ym01', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'Uhh...', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 14, null), ('cmpzj00dj002nlk0kotnftlxa', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 'CANDIDATE', 'मेरे जबन पड़ेगी क्या, मेरे से कौन मीटिंग आया?', '2026-06-04 13:23:17.863', 15, null), ('cmpz